[ac.blurb[0]] -> ARMOR CLASS (AC) reduces incoming physical
[ac.blurb[1]] -> attack damage by 1 for each point, up to a
[ac.blurb[2]] -> maximum of 75% of the total attack damage.
[ac.blurb[3]] -> While blocking, AC can reduce
[ac.blurb[4]] -> up to 100% physical damage.
[ac.details[0]] -> Stacking as much AC as possible may
[ac.details[1]] -> make an adventurer feel virtually
[ac.details[2]] -> impervious to attack, which is certainly
[ac.details[3]] -> a big advantage.
[ac.details[5]] -> However, the danger of most traps,
[ac.details[6]] -> magic, and status effects remain
[ac.details[7]] -> unimpeded by AC. Some enemy weapons
[ac.details[8]] -> are also designed specifically to
[ac.details[9]] -> penetrate armor.
[ac.details[11]] -> It is wise not to neglect AC, but
[ac.details[12]] -> take care not to be overconfident!
[alchemy skill.blurb[0]] -> With the aid of an alembic, alchemists can
[alchemy skill.blurb[1]] -> brew many kinds of potions, such as the
[alchemy skill.blurb[2]] -> unstable potions, which scale in power with
[alchemy skill.blurb[3]] -> skill. Drinking and throwing potions also
[alchemy skill.blurb[4]] -> practices the skill.
[alchemy skill.details[0]] -> While some skill can be gained by
[alchemy skill.details[1]] -> drinking and throwing potions, alchemy
[alchemy skill.details[2]] -> skill is truly practiced using an
[alchemy skill.details[3]] -> alembic.
[alchemy skill.details[5]] -> Combine any primary ingredient with a
[alchemy skill.details[6]] -> secondary ingredient to form a recipe.
[alchemy skill.details[7]] -> Each recipe learned improves skill.
[alchemy skill.details[9]] -> Keep empty bottles and tap sinks for
[alchemy skill.details[10]] -> healthy supplies of water for use in
[alchemy skill.details[11]] -> duplication, providing more chances
[alchemy skill.details[12]] -> to solve problems with potions.
[lore skill.blurb[0]] -> While any adventurer can see what an
[lore skill.blurb[1]] -> item is just by looking at it, skill in LORE
[lore skill.blurb[2]] -> can reveal important magical details.
[lore skill.blurb[3]] -> The more valuable the item, the more
[lore skill.blurb[4]] -> challenging it is to appraise.
[lore skill.blurb[5]] -> Skilled loremasters are great with song.
[lore skill.details[0]] -> As adventurers grow in Lore skill,
[lore skill.details[1]] -> manually managing which items are
[lore skill.details[2]] -> selected for appraisal can become
[lore skill.details[3]] -> more important. Higher value items
[lore skill.details[4]] -> may take much more time to identify.
[lore skill.details[5]] -> Focus on items that may be of actual
[lore skill.details[6]] -> use and discard the rest to spend
[lore skill.details[7]] -> less time fiddling with inventory.
[lore skill.details[9]] -> A few classes start with poor ability
[lore skill.details[10]] -> to appraise, thanks to very poor
[lore skill.details[11]] -> perception. Using unidentified potions
[lore skill.details[12]] -> or scrolls may yield an increase to
[lore skill.details[13]] -> lore skill, up to Basic (20) skill.
[axe skill.blurb[0]] -> A hefty axe provides bonus ATK on wooden
[axe skill.blurb[1]] -> objects, useful for breaking an obstacle in
[axe skill.blurb[2]] -> an emergency such as a locked door or
[axe skill.blurb[3]] -> stray mimic.
[axe skill.blurb[4]] -> A legend in AXE SKILL always causes foes
[axe skill.blurb[5]] -> to slow when dealing a legendary strike.
[axe skill.details[0]] -> Axes are a reliable, if unspecialized
[axe skill.details[1]] -> choice, with few enemies that can resist
[axe skill.details[2]] -> its hefty blade substantially.
[axe skill.details[4]] -> Its hacking power provides an extra
[axe skill.details[5]] -> point of guaranteed damage, making
[axe skill.details[6]] -> it great for general slaying, and
[axe skill.details[7]] -> chipping away at armored foes.
[backstabs.blurb[0]] -> To backstab an enemy, attack them in
[backstabs.blurb[1]] -> melee from behind while they are unaware
[backstabs.blurb[2]] -> of any threats, dealing greater damage.
[backstabs.blurb[3]] -> If the enemy is slain with this strike,
[backstabs.blurb[4]] -> it counts as an assassination!
[backstabs.details[0]] -> You can flee from a tougher fight,
[backstabs.details[1]] -> and then return to your prey after
[backstabs.details[2]] -> it has lost sight of you. Doing so gives
[backstabs.details[3]] -> you another chance to deal backstab
[backstabs.details[4]] -> damage and assassinate enemies
[backstabs.details[5]] -> whose health pool might otherwise be
[backstabs.details[6]] -> too large to cope with in a single bout.
[backstabs.details[8]] -> Consider using quickturn for the
[backstabs.details[9]] -> fastest possible escape!
[blocking.blurb[0]] -> When holding a shield or torch in their
[blocking.blurb[1]] -> off-hand, adventurers can deflect
[blocking.blurb[2]] -> incoming physical attacks, but the item
[blocking.blurb[3]] -> may be damaged. Higher skill improves
[blocking.blurb[4]] -> the amount of damage deflected.
[blocking.details[0]] -> While blocking, an adventurer can
[blocking.details[1]] -> fend off attacks from all sides.
[blocking.details[2]] -> If you decide you need to run, a
[blocking.details[3]] -> behind-the-back block can save your
[blocking.details[4]] -> life while you're retreating!
[blocking.details[6]] -> While usually it's a good idea to
[blocking.details[7]] -> block every melee attack, continuing
[blocking.details[8]] -> an assault and soaking an unblocked
[blocking.details[9]] -> hit may result in less overall damage.
[blocking.details[11]] -> Remember, AC doesn't block spell
[blocking.details[12]] -> damage, so only block against magic
[blocking.details[13]] -> if your shield has special properties.
[blocking skill.blurb[0]] -> BLOCKING SKILL provides additional armor
[blocking skill.blurb[1]] -> when wielding a shield, even when not
[blocking skill.blurb[2]] -> blocking. Legends in blocking skill can
[blocking skill.blurb[3]] -> deflect blows without degrading the item
[blocking skill.blurb[4]] -> used for blocking.
[blocking skill.details[0]] -> When seeking to improve your blocking
[blocking skill.details[1]] -> ability, the key is practice.
[blocking skill.details[3]] -> Avoid quick kills and carry backup
[blocking skill.details[4]] -> shields so that you can block as many
[blocking skill.details[5]] -> times as possible before vanquishing a
[blocking skill.details[6]] -> foe, without endangering yourself.
[blocking skill.details[8]] -> Training block skill with a torch can
[blocking skill.details[9]] -> only carry an adventurer to a max
[blocking skill.details[10]] -> skill of 40. After that, a shield is
[blocking skill.details[11]] -> needed to advance.
[chr.blurb[0]] -> Each point in CHARISMA (CHR) improves the
[chr.blurb[1]] -> trading rates with shopkeepers. It also
[chr.blurb[2]] -> improves follower speed, leadership skill,
[chr.blurb[3]] -> and charisma-based spells.
[chr.details[0]] -> Rather than putting one's self in
[chr.details[1]] -> harm's way, an adventurer with high
[chr.details[2]] -> CHARISMA has options for letting
[chr.details[3]] -> somebody else do the dirty work.
[chr.details[5]] -> The patron stat of the leadership skill,
[chr.details[6]] -> high CHR can offset inexperience,
[chr.details[7]] -> empowering early access to follower
[chr.details[8]] -> commands, and stronger charm spells.
[chr.details[10]] -> Also improving the trade skill, one
[chr.details[11]] -> should not underestimate the value of
[chr.details[12]] -> striking better deals with shops.
[chr.details[13]] -> Gaining early access to a shopkeeper's
[chr.details[14]] -> private stock can mean the difference
[chr.details[15]] -> between a great adventure and a
[chr.details[16]] -> desperate one.
[class.blurb[0]] -> A character's class determines their
[class.blurb[1]] -> starting skills, HP and MP/EN/ST,
[class.blurb[2]] -> equipment and spells, stats, and the
[class.blurb[3]] -> likelihood of each stat increasing
[class.blurb[4]] -> upon level up.
[class.details[0]] -> While most adventurers find success
[class.details[1]] -> playing to their strengths, some do
[class.details[2]] -> well by rounding out their weaknesses.
[class.details[4]] -> Resourcefulness may be more
[class.details[5]] -> important than raw ability, depending
[class.details[6]] -> on the situation.
[class.details[8]] -> When forming a party, work together
[class.details[9]] -> to select classes that will cover
[class.details[10]] -> one-another's weaknesses, or
[class.details[11]] -> enhance shared strengths.
[classes list.blurb[0]] -> Adventurers can adapt as they progress,
[classes list.blurb[1]] -> adopting skills and using equipment as
[classes list.blurb[2]] -> the dungeon's challenges may demand.
[classes list.blurb[3]] -> Still, class choice is essential to a
[classes list.blurb[4]] -> strong start, and ongoing growth.
[con.blurb[0]] -> Each point of CONSTITUTION (CON) adds
[con.blurb[1]] -> natural armor (AC). Those with high
[con.blurb[2]] -> constitution may recover from negative
[con.blurb[3]] -> status effects more quickly and restore
[con.blurb[4]] -> more health when healed.
[con.details[0]] -> Classes with strong CON growth may
[con.details[1]] -> find themselves able to make
[con.details[2]] -> equipment decisions based on benefits
[con.details[3]] -> without depending on AC added.
[con.details[5]] -> Those with low AC may prefer to
[con.details[6]] -> prioritize armor and protection
[con.details[7]] -> effects.
[con.details[9]] -> In both cases, AC remains important
[con.details[10]] -> for making sure you don't take too
[con.details[11]] -> much damage when struck by physical
[con.details[12]] -> attacks by foes.
[crits.blurb[0]] -> When making a melee attack, charge an
[crits.blurb[1]] -> attack until your arm begins to shake with
[crits.blurb[2]] -> tension. Releasing the attack at any point
[crits.blurb[3]] -> after that will result in a CRITICAL STRIKE,
[crits.blurb[4]] -> dealing additional damage!
[crits.details[0]] -> Your attack gains the benefit of a
[crits.details[1]] -> critical strike the instant your
[crits.details[2]] -> weapon begins to shake.
[crits.details[4]] -> Time your release to match your
[crits.details[5]] -> approach to the target. This is even
[crits.details[6]] -> more effective if the enemy's back
[crits.details[7]] -> is turned.
[crits.details[9]] -> It's not usually a good idea to
[crits.details[10]] -> continue performing critical strikes
[crits.details[11]] -> in the middle of a fight.
[dex.blurb[0]] -> Each point of DEXTERITY (DEX) improves
[dex.blurb[1]] -> an adventurer's potential movement speed,
[dex.blurb[2]] -> and enhances ranged attack (ATK) power.
[dex.details[0]] -> While every character may benefit
[dex.details[1]] -> from increased movement speed,
[dex.details[2]] -> characters who prefer to use ranged
[dex.details[3]] -> attacks will benefit from DEX the most.
[dex.details[5]] -> Dexterity improves ranged attacks,
[dex.details[6]] -> but improved speed also complements
[dex.details[7]] -> skirmishing. A fast adventurer can
[dex.details[8]] -> more easily stay out of enemy range,
[dex.details[9]] -> outrun traps, and dodge projectiles
[dex.details[10]] -> slung by foes.
[dex.details[12]] -> When you need to stay light on
[dex.details[13]] -> your feet DEX is essential!
[equipment degradation.blurb[0]] -> Most items have a chance to degrade upon
[equipment degradation.blurb[1]] -> use, whether taking a hit in armor,
[equipment degradation.blurb[2]] -> expending a charge on a magic item, or
[equipment degradation.blurb[3]] -> attacking with a weapon. Degraded items
[equipment degradation.blurb[4]] -> may perform worse than pristine ones.
[equipment degradation.details[0]] -> Opportunities to repair equipment
[equipment degradation.details[1]] -> may be rare or expensive, and
[equipment degradation.details[2]] -> equipment breakage during the
[equipment degradation.details[3]] -> middle of a fight can be deadly.
[equipment degradation.details[5]] -> Replacing your equipment regularly
[equipment degradation.details[6]] -> with items that are in better condition
[equipment degradation.details[7]] -> is usually a good idea.
[equipment degradation.details[9]] -> While tinkerers aren't blacksmiths,
[equipment degradation.details[10]] -> those who are very skilled may be
[equipment degradation.details[11]] -> able to patch up items for a cost.
[equipment degradation.details[12]] -> Scrolls of repair, though rare, are
[equipment degradation.details[13]] -> more reliable for most adventurers.
[flanking.blurb[0]] -> If an enemy is preoccupied in combat
[flanking.blurb[1]] -> against another foe, they have a harder
[flanking.blurb[2]] -> time defending themselves! Attack from
[flanking.blurb[3]] -> behind to gain additional flanking damage.
[flanking.details[0]] -> While a foe is focused on somebody
[flanking.details[1]] -> else, striking rapidly may be the
[flanking.details[2]] -> best way to bring down your target,
[flanking.details[3]] -> taking full advantage of extra
[flanking.details[4]] -> flanking damage.
[flanking.details[6]] -> Fighting solo, don't expect many
[flanking.details[7]] -> opportunities to flank. But when
[flanking.details[8]] -> adventuring with allies or followers,
[flanking.details[9]] -> one member of the party may very
[flanking.details[10]] -> often be gaining flanking benefits!
[hp.blurb[0]] -> HEALTH POINTS (HP) measure a denizen's
[hp.blurb[1]] -> vitality, with each point of damage
[hp.blurb[2]] -> removing 1 HP, and each point of healing
[hp.blurb[3]] -> restoring 1 HP. A denizen is slain when
[hp.blurb[4]] -> their HP is reduced to 0 or fewer.
[hp.details[0]] -> While a denizen's maximum HP increases
[hp.details[1]] -> substantially over the course of an
[hp.details[2]] -> adventure as they level up, their HP
[hp.details[3]] -> regeneration rate generally will not.
[hp.details[5]] -> As a result, it is important to continue
[hp.details[6]] -> minimizing HP loss in encounters and
[hp.details[7]] -> acquire means of HP restoration to
[hp.details[8]] -> recover from larger scrapes.
[int.blurb[0]] -> Each point of INTELLIGENCE (INT) improves
[int.blurb[1]] -> magic power and MP regeneration by a
[int.blurb[2]] -> percentage. It also contributes to magic
[int.blurb[3]] -> skills, allowing more difficult spells to
[int.blurb[4]] -> be memorized.
[int.details[0]] -> INT is great for improving magic ability
[int.details[1]] -> generally, enhancing RGN and PWR, and
[int.details[2]] -> making it easier to learn spells.
[int.details[4]] -> However, choosing items that directly
[int.details[5]] -> increase RGN or PWR may yield better
[int.details[6]] -> results than raw INT for focused
[int.details[7]] -> spellcasters.
[leadership skill.blurb[0]] -> An untrained adventurer can still gather
[leadership skill.blurb[1]] -> four followers, but they won't be able to
[leadership skill.blurb[2]] -> command them to do much. Higher levels of
[leadership skill.blurb[3]] -> LEADERSHIP SKILL grants access to many
[leadership skill.blurb[4]] -> useful commands.
[leadership skill.details[0]] -> Summons and recruited followers can
[leadership skill.details[1]] -> become quite strong if nurtured.
[leadership skill.details[2]] -> Allow them to get the last hit on
[leadership skill.details[3]] -> enemies, and you'll see their
[leadership skill.details[4]] -> confidence (and their levels) rise
[leadership skill.details[5]] -> dramatically!
[leadership skill.details[7]] -> Outfit them with ranged equipment,
[leadership skill.details[8]] -> keep healing spells on hand, and
[leadership skill.details[9]] -> distract / confuse enemies to keep
[leadership skill.details[10]] -> your loyal followers safe!
[leadership skill.details[12]] -> Wear a crown to inspire them further
[leadership skill.details[13]] -> with a variety of follower benefits.
[legendary strikes.blurb[0]] -> If an adventurer with LEGENDARY melee
[legendary strikes.blurb[1]] -> skill holds a critical strike until it
[legendary strikes.blurb[2]] -> releases on its own, they may gain an
[legendary strikes.blurb[3]] -> additional status effect against their
[legendary strikes.blurb[4]] -> victim. The effect depends on the weapon.
[legendary strikes.details[0]] -> Gaining enough skill points to reach
[legendary strikes.details[1]] -> legend in a melee skill may be tricky.
[legendary strikes.details[3]] -> If you are durable enough, avoid
[legendary strikes.details[4]] -> critical strikes so you can get more
[legendary strikes.details[5]] -> hits in, giving you more chances to
[legendary strikes.details[6]] -> increase your weapon skill.
[legendary strikes.details[8]] -> If legendary skill is developed, it
[legendary strikes.details[9]] -> may be available to save your life
[legendary strikes.details[10]] -> against the dungeon's fiercest foes.
[leveling up.blurb[0]] -> Whenever a character gains 100 XP,
[leveling up.blurb[1]] -> their level increases! When leveling
[leveling up.blurb[2]] -> up, every character receives the
[leveling up.blurb[3]] -> following: +5 Max HP, +5 Max MP,
[leveling up.blurb[4]] -> and an increase to 3 different stats.
[leveling up.details[0]] -> Each skill is based on a stat.
[leveling up.details[2]] -> If a stat increases upon leveling up,
[leveling up.details[3]] -> and skills associated with that stat
[leveling up.details[4]] -> have been practiced well, the increase
[leveling up.details[5]] -> may be for +2 points instead of +1.
[leveling up.details[7]] -> Use skills aligned with your class' stat
[leveling up.details[8]] -> growth to maximize your level-ups.
[mace skill.blurb[0]] -> Beating foes with a mace may break
[mace skill.blurb[1]] -> their armor more than with other weapons.
[mace skill.blurb[2]] -> A legend in MACE SKILL deals more damage
[mace skill.blurb[3]] -> and has a chance to inflict paralyze with
[mace skill.blurb[4]] -> a legendary strike.
[mace skill.details[0]] -> Don't be afraid to pick up and use a
[mace skill.details[1]] -> mace early in the dungeons, especially
[mace skill.details[2]] -> if you're using ranged weapons, magic,
[mace skill.details[3]] -> or swords.
[mace skill.details[5]] -> Its effectiveness at crushing undead
[mace skill.details[6]] -> may very well help you live long
[mace skill.details[7]] -> enough to become a master in other
[mace skill.details[8]] -> arts.
[melee.blurb[0]] -> Simply wield your fist or a melee weapon,
[melee.blurb[1]] -> such as a mace, spear, sword, or axe, and
[melee.blurb[2]] -> ATTACK! Fast strikes may allow an
[melee.blurb[3]] -> adventurer to slay a foe before it can
[melee.blurb[4]] -> respond with an attack of its own.
[melee.details[0]] -> A simple tap is enough to perform a
[melee.details[1]] -> full-strength melee strike.
[melee.details[3]] -> Only hold the attack longer if you
[melee.details[4]] -> need to time your strike, or if
[melee.details[5]] -> you're charging for a critical strike.
[melee.details[7]] -> When ambushing, adventurers often
[melee.details[8]] -> have time to follow-up a critical strike
[melee.details[9]] -> with one or two fast attacks. This is
[melee.details[10]] -> enough to finish off a lot of weaker
[melee.details[11]] -> enemies before they can even react.
[memorized.blurb[0]] -> Once memorized, spells can be readied
[memorized.blurb[1]] -> without the need for a spellbook.
[memorized.blurb[3]] -> MP, EN, and ST are consumed over the
[memorized.blurb[4]] -> course of the cast time, which will be
[memorized.blurb[5]] -> lost if the spell fizzles.
[memorized.details[0]] -> From your spell list, use the quickcast
[memorized.details[1]] -> option to immediately start casting the
[memorized.details[2]] -> spell without the need to equip it or
[memorized.details[3]] -> put it in your hotbar. For spells you
[memorized.details[4]] -> only need occasionally, this makes it
[memorized.details[5]] -> easier to keep essential spells ready.
[memorized.details[7]] -> Unless you want to use a book for
[memorized.details[8]] -> enhanced PWR, books can safely be
[memorized.details[9]] -> discarded or sold once a spell is
[memorized.details[10]] -> memorized. Be careful to avoid
[memorized.details[11]] -> reading cursed spellbooks, which will
[memorized.details[12]] -> result in forgetting a random spell!
[missiles.blurb[0]] -> Slingshots, crossbows, and bows fire
[missiles.blurb[1]] -> MISSILES when used to attack. These
[missiles.blurb[2]] -> weapons may take time to load before the
[missiles.blurb[3]] -> attack fires. Crossbows and bows can be
[missiles.blurb[4]] -> loaded with special ammo when it is
[missiles.blurb[5]] -> held in the off-hand.
[missiles.details[0]] -> Augment crossbows and bows with
[missiles.details[1]] -> special ammo to increase your
[missiles.details[2]] -> damage output and inflict debilitating
[missiles.details[3]] -> status effects on dangerous targets.
[missiles.details[5]] -> Enemies will always know where a
[missiles.details[6]] -> ranged weapon attack came from
[missiles.details[7]] -> when struck. Use this to lure your
[missiles.details[8]] -> foes where you want them.
[missiles.details[10]] -> Many foes are resistant to small
[missiles.details[11]] -> projectiles, but your ability to
[missiles.details[12]] -> hit-and-run will give you the time you
[missiles.details[13]] -> need to chip their HP down.
[mp.blurb[0]] -> Casting memorized spells, or spells from
[mp.blurb[1]] -> books, requires MAGIC POINTS (MP),
[mp.blurb[2]] -> ENERGY (EN), or STEAM (ST). Casters usually
[mp.blurb[3]] -> must have a quantity equal to or greater
[mp.blurb[4]] -> than the cost of the spell in order to cast.
[mp.details[0]] -> If MP seems too scarce, finish off foes
[mp.details[1]] -> that are close to death without magic.
[mp.details[2]] -> Save gold for shops, which may sell
[mp.details[3]] -> potions that restore magic points.
[mp.details[5]] -> VAMPIRE BLOOD MAGIC:
[mp.details[6]] -> Vampires can continue casting when
[mp.details[7]] -> their MP is empty, consuming HP
[mp.details[8]] ->  instead.
[mp.details[9]] -> Take care with channeled spells!
[mp.details[11]] -> AUTOMATON STEAM:
[mp.details[12]] -> Steam regeneration depends on the
[mp.details[13]] -> heat of the automaton's boiler. Some
[mp.details[14]] -> fuels can cause it to super-heat,
[mp.details[15]] -> resulting in rapid steam build-up. If a
[mp.details[16]] -> boiler is cold, steam will depressurize
[mp.details[17]] -> ultimately killing the automaton.
[mp.details[19]] -> INSECTOID ENERGY:
[mp.details[20]] -> Insectoids metabolize energy into
[mp.details[21]] -> magic, but can only eat so much.
[mp.details[22]] -> Their energy pool is capped and
[mp.details[23]] -> doesn't regenerate, but they can eat
[mp.details[24]] -> all foods to rapidly regain energy
[mp.details[25]] -> used in casting.
[mp.details[26]] -> Magic potions and fruit juice also
[mp.details[27]] -> restore lots of energy.
[per.blurb[0]] -> PERCEPTION (PER) improves visibility in
[per.blurb[1]] -> darkness and increases appraisal.
[per.blurb[3]] -> PER also increases the likelihood that
[per.blurb[4]] -> ranged attacks will pierce 50% of a
[per.blurb[5]] -> target's armor.
[per.details[0]] -> PER is essential for characters
[per.details[1]] -> focused on missile weapons, making
[per.details[2]] -> tough enemies more susceptible to
[per.details[3]] -> ranged attacks.
[per.details[5]] -> Tinkering and appraise skills also
[per.details[6]] -> benefit from a strong perception stat.
[per.details[8]] -> If you're struggling to appraise, a
[per.details[9]] -> little boost to PER can make all
[per.details[10]] -> the difference.
[polearm skill.blurb[0]] -> Polearms strikes are more accurate,
[polearm skill.blurb[1]] -> with reduced damage variance compared
[polearm skill.blurb[2]] -> to other melee skills of similar level.
[polearm skill.blurb[3]] -> A legend in POLEARM SKILL always causes
[polearm skill.blurb[4]] -> Knockback when dealing a legendary
[polearm skill.blurb[5]] -> strike.
[polearm skill.details[0]] -> The polearm is a popular choice for
[polearm skill.details[1]] -> many classes.
[polearm skill.details[3]] -> Due to its general effectiveness
[polearm skill.details[4]] -> against human-sized targets, it's
[polearm skill.details[5]] -> generally an all-around great
[polearm skill.details[6]] -> starter weapon.
[polearm skill.details[8]] -> Watch out for certain big monsters,
[polearm skill.details[9]] -> or tiny ones, who may be difficult to
[polearm skill.details[10]] -> skewer.
[pwr.blurb[0]] -> A denizen's MAGIC POWER (PWR) improves
[pwr.blurb[1]] -> the spells they cast by percentage,
[pwr.blurb[2]] -> increasing damage output, healing, or
[pwr.blurb[3]] -> status effect duration.
[pwr.details[0]] -> Some spells have a binary effect, and
[pwr.details[1]] -> as a result, PWR won't influence every
[pwr.details[2]] -> spell.
[pwr.details[4]] -> But for damaging and healing spells,
[pwr.details[5]] -> PWR is extremely useful, particularly
[pwr.details[6]] -> when casting from a blessed book.
[pwr.details[8]] -> Status effects may increase in
[pwr.details[9]] -> duration with improved PWR.
[races.blurb[0]] -> Humans aren't the only intelligent
[races.blurb[1]] -> creatures in the dungeons. RACES each
[races.blurb[2]] -> have their own friends and foes.
[races.blurb[3]] -> They also have starting abilities,
[races.blurb[4]] -> resistances, food preferences,
[races.blurb[5]] -> and penalties.
[races.details[0]] -> Most races can recruit their own kind.
[races.details[1]] -> While human shopkeepers will
[races.details[2]] -> attack threats on sight, salamanders,
[races.details[3]] -> myconids, dryads, gnomes, and
[races.details[4]] -> automatons are welcome in shops.
[races.details[6]] -> When selecting your race, use
[races.details[7]] -> the "Show Race Info" button to
[races.details[8]] -> reveal all strengths, weaknesses,
[races.details[9]] -> abilities, and allegiances.
[races.details[10]] -> To make the dungeons easier, pair
[races.details[11]] -> each race with a class that minimizes
[races.details[12]] -> the downsides, and doubles-down on
[races.details[13]] -> the benefits.
[ranged skill.blurb[0]] -> Pelting enemies with missiles may result
[ranged skill.blurb[1]] -> in penetrating their armor. Legendary
[ranged skill.blurb[2]] -> ranged skill allows an archer to use
[ranged skill.blurb[3]] -> missile weapons without degrading
[ranged skill.blurb[4]] -> their quality.
[ranged skill.details[0]] -> Using low-damage missile weapons like
[ranged skill.details[1]] -> the slingshot or short bow is a reliable
[ranged skill.details[2]] -> way to raise your skill, considering
[ranged skill.details[3]] -> how many shots it might take to bring
[ranged skill.details[4]] -> down an enemy.
[ranged skill.details[6]] -> However, the dungeons often won't be
[ranged skill.details[7]] -> generous, with few safe spaces to run
[ranged skill.details[8]] -> and kite.
[ranged skill.details[10]] -> Take care to ensure survival is your
[ranged skill.details[11]] -> top priority when training.
[res.blurb[0]] -> Magic damage ignores AC, but MAGIC RESIST
[res.blurb[1]] -> (RES) will reduce the amount of damage
[res.blurb[2]] -> taken by a percentage. The duration of
[res.blurb[3]] -> negative magic status effects is also
[res.blurb[4]] -> reduced.
[res.details[0]] -> Since AC won't reduce the damage
[res.details[1]] -> taken from spells, it's a good idea to
[res.details[2]] -> look for sources of magic resistance.
[res.details[4]] -> Magic reflect completely negates
[res.details[5]] -> magic projectiles, but comes at a cost.
[res.details[6]] -> Resistance, by comparison, is passive
[res.details[7]] -> and reliable.
[res.details[9]] -> Some races have a natural resistance
[res.details[10]] -> or vulnerability to magic attacks.
[rgn.blurb[0]] -> Most denizens regenerate over time,
[rgn.blurb[1]] -> restoring lost HP and MP. Increasing
[rgn.blurb[2]] -> REGENERATION (RGN) improves how fast
[rgn.blurb[3]] -> these are restored.
[rgn.details[0]] -> While HP and MP can be depleted very
[rgn.details[1]] -> rapidly, a little practice can help get
[rgn.details[2]] -> an adventurer comfortable with how
[rgn.details[3]] -> long they take to restore.
[rgn.details[5]] -> Explore, manage inventory, and stay
[rgn.details[6]] -> away from threats when you are
[rgn.details[7]] -> depleted, allowing you to benefit fully
[rgn.details[8]] -> from RGN.
[rgn.details[10]] -> Note that HP regen is disabled with
[rgn.details[11]] -> the hunger Game Setting turned off.
[skills.blurb[0]] -> Many actions that adventurers take will
[skills.blurb[1]] -> be modified by the level of their SKILLS.
[skills.blurb[3]] -> As they continue practicing, skills
[skills.blurb[4]] -> will increase organically, sometimes
[skills.blurb[5]] -> unlocking entirely new capabilities.
[skills.details[0]] -> A class' starting skills can be an
[skills.details[1]] -> excellent guide to how to most
[skills.details[2]] -> effectively succeed as that class.
[skills.details[4]] -> In some cases, classes have skills that
[skills.details[5]] -> they lack the equipment to use, which
[skills.details[6]] -> might motivate a hunt for certain
[skills.details[7]] -> items.
[skills.details[9]] -> Every skill has a new capability that's
[skills.details[10]] -> unlocked once the skill reaches
[skills.details[11]] -> legendary status (100).
[sneaking.blurb[0]] -> With nothing, or special ammo, held in the
[sneaking.blurb[1]] -> off-hand, an adventurer can creep slowly,
[sneaking.blurb[2]] -> making it harder for foes to detect them.
[sneaking.blurb[3]] -> Careful SNEAKING also makes it easier to
[sneaking.blurb[4]] -> see in the shadows.
[sneaking.details[0]] -> When feeling constantly beset or
[sneaking.details[1]] -> surprised by foes, consider how much
[sneaking.details[2]] -> light sources are exposing you.
[sneaking.details[4]] -> When taking advantage of darkness
[sneaking.details[5]] -> and sneaking, all but the most
[sneaking.details[6]] -> specialized hunters have a hard
[sneaking.details[7]] -> time finding a stealthy adventurer.
[spellbook casting.blurb[0]] -> Any adventurer can wield a spellbook
[spellbook casting.blurb[1]] -> in their off-hand and attempt to cast
[spellbook casting.blurb[2]] -> the spell within. Adventurers with high
[spellbook casting.blurb[3]] -> INT will gain an additional PWR bonus
[spellbook casting.blurb[4]] -> when casting from the book compared to
[spellbook casting.blurb[5]] -> casting from memory.
[spellbook casting.details[0]] -> Dedicated magicians may benefit from
[spellbook casting.details[1]] -> keeping their favorite attack spell
[spellbook casting.details[2]] -> at ready with a wielded spellbook.
[spellbook casting.details[4]] -> In addition to providing greater PWR,
[spellbook casting.details[5]] -> another memorized spell can also be
[spellbook casting.details[6]] -> readied, permitting immediate access
[spellbook casting.details[7]] -> to multiple magic solutions.
[spellbook casting.details[9]] -> Off-hand spellbooks can be blessed
[spellbook casting.details[10]] -> like any equipment, providing huge
[spellbook casting.details[11]] -> bonuses to the book's PWR. Use an
[spellbook casting.details[12]] -> enchanted feather to repair a
[spellbook casting.details[13]] -> spellbook you depend on!
[stats metastats.blurb[0]] -> Stats measure a character's capabilities
[stats metastats.blurb[1]] -> and are at the root of each skill. These
[stats metastats.blurb[2]] -> include STR, CON, DEX, INT, PER, CHR.
[stats metastats.blurb[3]] -> Metastats such as PWR, AC, RGN and ATK
[stats metastats.blurb[4]] -> are not raised directly by leveling up.
[stats metastats.details[0]] -> Each adventurer may find some stats
[stats metastats.details[1]] -> more essential than others. It's wise
[stats metastats.details[2]] -> to monitor your character sheet and
[stats metastats.details[3]] -> collect the kind of equipment that
[stats metastats.details[4]] -> benefits your most useful stats.
[stats metastats.details[6]] -> Pay attention to the skill sheet where
[stats metastats.details[7]] -> the governing stat is shown. High stats
[stats metastats.details[8]] -> can sometimes compensate for poor
[stats metastats.details[9]] -> skill.
[stats metastats.details[11]] -> Metastats are not based on level or
[stats metastats.details[12]] -> class but are instead a combination of
[stats metastats.details[13]] -> stats, skills, levels, and equipment.
[stealth skill.blurb[0]] -> High STEALTH SKILL makes it easier to hide
[stealth skill.blurb[1]] -> from foes and improves the damage caused
[stealth skill.blurb[2]] -> by backstabs and flanking strikes.
[stealth skill.blurb[4]] -> Legends in stealth can become almost
[stealth skill.blurb[5]] -> invisible on a whim.
[stealth skill.details[0]] -> When creeping through the dungeons,
[stealth skill.details[1]] -> pause when you see a foe. If you take
[stealth skill.details[2]] -> an extra moment to let your enemy
[stealth skill.details[3]] -> look away, you can rush in for a
[stealth skill.details[4]] -> backstab, or even assassination!
[stealth skill.details[6]] -> These actions have a higher likelihood
[stealth skill.details[7]] -> of increasing your stealth skill.
[stealth skill.details[8]] -> With dedication to melee ambushing
[stealth skill.details[9]] -> tactics, an adventurer can become
[stealth skill.details[10]] -> a legend in their stealth ability.
[str.blurb[0]] -> Each point of STRENGTH (STR) adds to
[str.blurb[1]] -> melee attack (ATK) power. Strong
[str.blurb[2]] -> adventurers can also carry heavier
[str.blurb[3]] -> equipment, and lug more in their
[str.blurb[4]] -> inventory, without being slowed.
[str.details[0]] -> A character who depends primarily on
[str.details[1]] -> melee attacks will always benefit
[str.details[2]] -> from more STR.
[str.details[4]] -> Prioritize gear blessed with STR
[str.details[5]] -> bonuses to further enhance your
[str.details[6]] -> melee power.
[strafing.blurb[0]] -> When exploring, adventurers move
[strafing.blurb[1]] -> confidently forward at full speed,
[strafing.blurb[2]] -> but stepping backward or to the side
[strafing.blurb[3]] -> is slower. This is important to know
[strafing.blurb[4]] -> when dealing with threats you
[strafing.blurb[5]] -> don't want to be near.
[strafing.details[0]] -> While you might be tempted to back
[strafing.details[1]] -> away from an intimidating foe, or
[strafing.details[2]] -> sidestep away from a boulder, it is
[strafing.details[3]] -> much faster to turn and run!
[strafing.details[5]] -> Many adventurers have been smashed
[strafing.details[6]] -> because they were caught staring,
[strafing.details[7]] -> at the source of their demise.
[strafing.details[9]] -> Use the quickturn button if
[strafing.details[10]] -> you have trouble turning fast!
[sword skill.blurb[0]] -> Slashing against foes with a sword
[sword skill.blurb[1]] -> increases the chance they may bleed. A
[sword skill.blurb[2]] -> legend in SWORD SKILL always causes bleed
[sword skill.blurb[3]] -> when dealing a legendary strike.
[sword skill.details[0]] -> Swords may seem weak at first, as
[sword skill.details[1]] -> Skeletons are very resistant to the
[sword skill.details[2]] -> sword's honed edge.
[sword skill.details[4]] -> As you encounter more foes, you'll
[sword skill.details[5]] -> discover that some tough enemies are
[sword skill.details[6]] -> quite vulnerable to the blade.
[sword skill.details[8]] -> Be patient and careful as a novice
[sword skill.details[9]] -> swordsman.
[thrown.blurb[0]] -> Thrown weapon attacks pierce armor
[thrown.blurb[1]] -> and gain increased damage from DEX.
[thrown.blurb[3]] -> Charging a THROWN ATTACK improves
[thrown.blurb[4]] -> its flight distance and damage
[thrown.blurb[5]] -> considerably.
[thrown.details[0]] -> Thrown weapon attacks can quickly
[thrown.details[1]] -> take down otherwise tough enemies,
[thrown.details[2]] -> with 50% reduction to target AC.
[thrown.details[4]] -> Having to collect your items after,
[thrown.details[5]] -> or even during, the fight means you
[thrown.details[6]] -> must remain vigilant and careful with
[thrown.details[7]] -> your inventory.
[thrown.details[9]] -> Prepare to disable enemies or sneak
[thrown.details[10]] -> away to make sure you can have your
[thrown.details[11]] -> bandolier full for an encounter.
[tinkering skill.blurb[0]] -> With only a lockpick, a talented tinkerer
[tinkering skill.blurb[1]] -> can accomplish quite a lot. But the real
[tinkering skill.blurb[2]] -> power of tinkering is accessed with a
[tinkering skill.blurb[3]] -> tinkering kit. For every problem,
[tinkering skill.blurb[4]] -> tinkerers have a mechanical solution.
[tinkering skill.details[0]] -> After grasping the basics learned
[tinkering skill.details[1]] -> from scrapping items at Expert (60)
[tinkering skill.details[2]] -> skill level, raising tinkering can be a
[tinkering skill.details[3]] -> challenge.
[tinkering skill.details[5]] -> Construct as many traps as possible
[tinkering skill.details[6]] -> and let sentries get the final hit on
[tinkering skill.details[7]] -> enemies to improve your odds of
[tinkering skill.details[8]] -> increasing tinkering skill.
[tinkering skill.details[10]] -> When burdened with excess scrap, use
[tinkering skill.details[11]] -> flame/freeze traps and beartraps as
[tinkering skill.details[12]] -> a primary means of attack, which may
[tinkering skill.details[13]] -> also grant increases to tinkering skill.
[trading skill.blurb[0]] -> TRADING SKILL helps an adventurer get
[trading skill.blurb[1]] -> the most out of their gold, buying or
[trading skill.blurb[2]] -> selling. Only a skilled tradesman can
[trading skill.blurb[3]] -> convince them to part with a shopkeeper's
[trading skill.blurb[4]] -> private reserve of consumables.
[trading skill.details[0]] -> Trade skill will only increase when
[trading skill.details[1]] -> purchasing items, with each item's gold
[trading skill.details[2]] -> cost amounting to the chance that the
[trading skill.details[3]] -> trade skill will increase (up to 100).
[trading skill.details[5]] -> In other words, items costing 100 gold
[trading skill.details[6]] -> have a 100% chance of increasing skill.
[trading skill.details[8]] -> A shop's private stock is a great
[trading skill.details[9]] -> source of items that have a good
[trading skill.details[10]] -> likelihood of upping your skill while
[trading skill.details[11]] -> also often being useful to keep on
[trading skill.details[12]] -> hand. A new private stock item becomes
[trading skill.details[13]] -> available every 10 skill levels up to 40.
[unarmed skill.blurb[0]] -> Those with high UNARMED SKILL may knock
[unarmed skill.blurb[1]] -> back foes with critical strikes. Those
[unarmed skill.blurb[2]] -> with legendary ability may briefly
[unarmed skill.blurb[3]] -> paralyze a foe with a powerful
[unarmed skill.blurb[4]] -> legendary strike from behind.
[unarmed skill.details[0]] -> While overall dealing less damage, and
[unarmed skill.details[1]] -> being less effective against many
[unarmed skill.details[2]] -> targets, a tough fighter can quickly
[unarmed skill.details[3]] -> increase their skill in unarmed
[unarmed skill.details[4]] -> fighting.
[unarmed skill.details[6]] -> This is thanks in part to how many hits
[unarmed skill.details[7]] -> it may take to bring down a foe.
[unarmed skill.details[9]] -> With great skill, an unarmed fighting
[unarmed skill.details[10]] -> master is a serious threat with fewer
[unarmed skill.details[11]] -> needs.
[wanted.blurb[0]] -> If an adventurer is WANTED by the
[wanted.blurb[1]] -> Merchants' Guild, shopkeepers will attack
[wanted.blurb[2]] -> them on sight. Qualities like race, certain
[wanted.blurb[3]] -> items, or magic effects might change how
[wanted.blurb[4]] -> shopkeepers feel about you as a customer.
[wanted.details[0]] -> Shopkeepers are tough enough that
[wanted.details[1]] -> attacking them is already a risky
[wanted.details[2]] -> prospect, but making all of them
[wanted.details[3]] -> hostile has great opportunity cost.
[wanted.details[5]] -> With certain resources, it's possible to
[wanted.details[6]] -> get away with robbing shops only to
[wanted.details[7]] -> come back later as a customer.
[wanted.details[9]] -> Use a bandit mask to mug shopkeepers
[wanted.details[10]] -> and remove it when finished. If your
[wanted.details[11]] -> real identity is wanted, use the
[wanted.details[12]] -> charm spell to convince shopkeepers
[wanted.details[13]] -> to forgive your crimes.
[weapon quality.blurb[0]] -> All weapons do less damage when they
[weapon quality.blurb[1]] -> are in poorer condition. High Tinkering
[weapon quality.blurb[2]] -> skill and Scrolls of Repair can be used
[weapon quality.blurb[3]] -> to improve weapon damage to its greatest
[weapon quality.blurb[4]] -> potential.
[weapon quality.details[0]] -> All melee and ranged weapons lose ATK
[weapon quality.details[1]] -> when they degrade in quality.
[weapon quality.details[3]] -> Don't over-commit to a damaged
[weapon quality.details[4]] -> weapon.
[weapon quality.details[6]] -> Even if it's blessed, you might find a
[weapon quality.details[7]] -> fresh, mundane weapon that
[weapon quality.details[8]] -> significantly outclasses a weapon
[weapon quality.details[9]] -> that's about to break.
[weapon quality.details[11]] -> If you hope to repair your favorite
[weapon quality.details[12]] -> weapon, a mundane backup is a good
[weapon quality.details[13]] -> idea too.
[wgt.blurb[0]] -> Each item equipped or held in the inventory
[wgt.blurb[1]] -> adds WEIGHT (WGT). Higher STR allows an
[wgt.blurb[2]] -> adventurer to carry more WGT before it
[wgt.blurb[3]] -> slows them. The more WGT, the greater the
[wgt.blurb[4]] -> speed penalty.
[wgt.details[0]] -> Many adventurers make the mistake
[wgt.details[1]] -> of collecting every item they see
[wgt.details[2]] -> which leads to high weight and slow
[wgt.details[3]] -> movement speed.
[wgt.details[5]] -> This invites death.
[wgt.details[7]] -> It's usually wise to throw items away
[wgt.details[8]] -> you don't think you'll use in the next
[wgt.details[9]] -> next few minutes, just to stay light on
[wgt.details[10]] -> your feet.
[xp.blurb[0]] -> Whenever a character's skill increases,
[xp.blurb[1]] -> they gain 2 EXPERIENCE POINTS (XP). Killing
[xp.blurb[2]] -> monsters will also yield XP based on the
[xp.blurb[3]] -> challenge of the kill.
[xp.blurb[5]] -> Gain 100 XP to level up!
[xp.details[0]] -> If you have the time, seek monsters
[xp.details[1]] -> to slay and opportunities to practice
[xp.details[2]] -> different skills to increase your XP.
[xp.details[3]] -> Descending too quickly without
[xp.details[4]] -> earning enough levels is likely
[xp.details[5]] -> to end in death!
[xp.details[7]] -> Combat XP is split between all players
[xp.details[8]] -> when adventuring together.
[xp.details[10]] -> If you already have a skill maxed out,
[xp.details[11]] -> consider training a different skill so
[xp.details[12]] -> you can keep gaining experience.
[sorcery skill.blurb[0]] -> The SORCERY SKILL allows casters to
[sorcery skill.blurb[1]] -> learn more advanced Sorcery spells and
[sorcery skill.blurb[2]] -> increases PWR using them.
[sorcery skill.blurb[3]] -> A Legend in Sorcery has increased
[sorcery skill.blurb[4]] -> casting speeds and even greater PWR
[sorcery skill.blurb[5]] -> while using their Sorcery spells.
[sorcery skill.details[0]] -> Sorcery is the most direct of all
[sorcery skill.details[1]] -> magic disciplines for adventuring.
[sorcery skill.details[2]] -> No other school provides such
[sorcery skill.details[3]] -> prolific access to combat spells
[sorcery skill.details[4]] -> at all levels of skill. In addition,
[sorcery skill.details[5]] -> powerful utility and defensive magic
[sorcery skill.details[6]] -> are found in the sorcerer's grimoire.
[sorcery skill.details[8]] -> Like all magic users, sorcerers
[sorcery skill.details[9]] -> should trade out spells as they grow
[sorcery skill.details[10]] -> in skill. But they'll do well to
[sorcery skill.details[11]] -> remember their most reliable spells
[sorcery skill.details[12]] -> when facing greater challenges.
[thaumaturgy skill.blurb[0]] -> The THAUMATURGY SKILL allows casters
[thaumaturgy skill.blurb[1]] -> to learn more advanced Thaumaturgy
[thaumaturgy skill.blurb[2]] -> spells and increases PWR using them.
[thaumaturgy skill.blurb[3]] -> A Legend in Thaumaturgy has increased
[thaumaturgy skill.blurb[4]] -> casting speeds and even greater PWR
[thaumaturgy skill.blurb[5]] -> while using their Thaumaturgy spells.
[thaumaturgy skill.details[0]] -> The preferred school for devout
[thaumaturgy skill.details[1]] -> adventurers, thaumaturges provide
[thaumaturgy skill.details[2]] -> protection, restoration, and access to
[thaumaturgy skill.details[3]] -> divine wisdom or providence. These
[thaumaturgy skill.details[4]] -> offer assistance both to individual
[thaumaturgy skill.details[5]] -> adventurers and their parties.
[thaumaturgy skill.details[7]] -> Though most reliable for utility uses,
[thaumaturgy skill.details[8]] -> some spells offer divine wrath against
[thaumaturgy skill.details[9]] -> undead and demonic foes.
[thaumaturgy skill.details[11]] -> Thaumaturges tend to succeed when
[thaumaturgy skill.details[12]] -> magic is used to supplement other
[thaumaturgy skill.details[13]] -> practical adventuring skills.
[mysticism skill.blurb[0]] -> The MYSTICISM SKILL allows casters
[mysticism skill.blurb[1]] -> to learn more advanced Mysticism
[mysticism skill.blurb[2]] -> spells and increases PWR using them.
[mysticism skill.blurb[3]] -> A Legend in Mysticism has increased
[mysticism skill.blurb[4]] -> casting speeds and even greater PWR
[mysticism skill.blurb[5]] -> while using their Mysticism spells.
[mysticism skill.details[0]] -> Spells available to mystics tend to
[mysticism skill.details[1]] -> provide methods of control. Though
[mysticism skill.details[2]] -> often indirect compared to the other
[mysticism skill.details[3]] -> schools, a successful mystic prefers
[mysticism skill.details[4]] -> to create and exploit opportunity.
[mysticism skill.details[6]] -> While not as reliable as sorcery for
[mysticism skill.details[7]] -> combat spells, mysticism attack spells
[mysticism skill.details[8]] -> may open up or pay off on other kinds
[mysticism skill.details[9]] -> of opportunities to devastating effect.
[mysticism skill.details[11]] -> Mysticism reliably allows dominion
[mysticism skill.details[12]] -> over objects and minds for the
[mysticism skill.details[13]] -> more strategic adventurer.
[offhand casting.blurb[0]] -> Different kinds of magic items can be
[offhand casting.blurb[1]] -> held for OFF-HAND CASTING, allowing the
[offhand casting.blurb[2]] -> wielder to channel a magic effect.
[offhand casting.blurb[3]] -> Channeling may rapidly recast the item's
[offhand casting.blurb[4]] -> effect, or build up a spell's charge,
[offhand casting.blurb[5]] -> until channeling is released.
[offhand casting.details[0]] -> Three categories of off-hand casting
[offhand casting.details[1]] -> items align with the three main schools
[offhand casting.details[2]] -> of magic. These benefit the spells cast
[offhand casting.details[3]] -> from that school with additional PWR,
[offhand casting.details[4]] -> but they also provide their own magic
[offhand casting.details[5]] -> effects. The fourth category benefits
[offhand casting.details[6]] -> from the Lore skill.
[offhand casting.details[8]] -> SOURCE FOCI:
[offhand casting.details[9]] -> Particularly for sorcerers who like
[offhand casting.details[10]] -> to keep cleverer spells prepared, an
[offhand casting.details[11]] -> elemental source focus provides fast
[offhand casting.details[12]] -> access to quick blasts of damage.
[offhand casting.details[14]] -> HOLY SYMBOL:
[offhand casting.details[15]] -> Carried faithfully by thaumaturges,
[offhand casting.details[16]] -> holy symbols reward preparation with
[offhand casting.details[17]] -> largely preventative benefits.
[offhand casting.details[19]] -> DARK ICON:
[offhand casting.details[20]] -> Ideal for when one might have allies
[offhand casting.details[21]] -> to buy time in a fight, dark icons
[offhand casting.details[22]] -> afflict powerful curses at some
[offhand casting.details[23]] -> distance. The curse applies to an
[offhand casting.details[24]] -> area, potentially giving greater
[offhand casting.details[25]] -> control over enemy combatants.
[offhand casting.details[27]] -> BARD INSTRUMENTS:
[offhand casting.details[28]] -> Continually adding powerful buffs
[offhand casting.details[29]] -> to the player and any nearby allies
[offhand casting.details[30]] -> or followers, Lore and Charisma aids
