[arcane citadel.details[10]] -> A good source of dig and the open spell
[arcane citadel.details[11]] -> can simplify exploration considerably.
[arcane citadel.details[13]] -> Take care not to be cornered by large
[arcane citadel.details[14]] -> enemies like the cockatrice and golem.
[arrow trap.blurb[0]] -> First thought to be created by goblins,
[arrow trap.blurb[1]] -> these complex mechanisms are now known
[arrow trap.blurb[2]] -> to predate them.
[arrow trap.blurb[4]] -> However, they have been repurposed by
[arrow trap.blurb[5]] -> resourceful goblin craftsfolk.
[arrow trap.details[0]] -> Unless the dungeon is unnaturally,
[arrow trap.details[1]] -> dark, arrow traps always have two
[arrow trap.details[2]] -> torches fixed to the face.
[arrow trap.details[4]] -> Each trap is filled with a random
[arrow trap.details[5]] -> type of ammo to afflict their target.
[arrow trap.details[6]] -> This ammo can be pilfered using a
[arrow trap.details[7]] -> lockpick, if the user is skilled
[arrow trap.details[8]] -> in tinkering, disabling the trap.
[arrow trap.details[10]] -> Arrow traps may also be disarmed
[arrow trap.details[11]] -> by tossing an item in front of the trap.
[arrow trap.details[12]] -> They can only fire arrows five times.
[bell.blurb[0]] -> Many towns and cities make use of BELLS
[bell.blurb[1]] -> to draw the attention of inhabitants,
[bell.blurb[2]] -> lifting spirits for collective events.
[bell.blurb[4]] -> Old bells that haven't been maintained
[bell.blurb[5]] -> will sometimes fail spectacularly.
[bell.details[0]] -> FOUND IN:
[bell.details[1]] -> - The Ruins
[bell.details[2]] -> - The Citadel
[bell.details[4]] -> BELL USE EFFECTS:
[bell.details[5]] -> - Stamina (1 Minute)
[bell.details[6]] -> - Agility (1 Minute)
[bell.details[7]] -> - Mentality (1 Minute)
[bell.details[8]] -> - Strength (1 Minute)
[bell.details[9]] -> - HP/MP Restoration
[bell.details[10]] -> - Attracts NPCs within 15 tiles
[bell.details[12]] -> SPAWN POSSIBILITIES:
[bell.details[13]] -> - 25% Spellbook hidden inside
[bell.details[14]] -> - 25% Gold hidden inside
[bell.details[15]] -> - 25% Bats hidden inside
[bell.details[17]] -> It's usually a good idea to ring a bell,
[bell.details[18]] -> if you're not afraid of a fight!
[bell.details[19]] -> Each bell will always provide the same
[bell.details[20]] -> effect to those who are close enough
[bell.details[21]] -> to be inspired by its song. Standing so
[bell.details[22]] -> close is not without risk, as bats may
[bell.details[23]] -> spill out or the structure may fail
[bell.details[24]] -> unexpectedly!
[bell.details[26]] -> Falling bells deal 80 damage to those
[bell.details[27]] -> caught in it's path. The low-hanging
[bell.details[28]] -> bell can also be used to deal damage
[bell.details[29]] -> to an over-confident minotaur.
[boulder trap.blurb[0]] -> Heralded by dark holes in the ceiling,
[boulder trap.blurb[1]] -> some say the huge stones are the result
[boulder trap.blurb[2]] -> of cave-ins from excavated earth.
[boulder trap.blurb[4]] -> Others theorize that they are a
[boulder trap.blurb[5]] -> punishment from the gods themselves.
[boulder trap.details[0]] -> Boulders deal 80 damage, regardless
[boulder trap.details[1]] -> of the victim's armor or constitution.
[boulder trap.details[2]] -> If they're not killed by a boulder, it
[boulder trap.details[3]] -> will shatter into several rocks.
[boulder trap.details[5]] -> Boulders will only roll straight
[boulder trap.details[6]] -> North, South, East or West.
[boulder trap.details[8]] -> Boulders that would block the exit
[boulder trap.details[9]] -> are shattered by the gods, leaving
[boulder trap.details[10]] -> behind a lucky rock in its rubble.
[boulder trap.details[12]] -> Most boulder traps can be triggered
[boulder trap.details[13]] -> by throwing an object under the hole.
[brams castle.blurb[0]] -> While inaccessible by mundane means,
[brams castle.blurb[1]] -> this manor lies somewhere in the depths
[brams castle.blurb[2]] -> of the Citadel's machinery. It seems that
[brams castle.blurb[3]] -> immortals like their own spaces away
[brams castle.blurb[4]] -> from prying eyes.
[brams castle.details[0]] -> SECRET LEVEL TREASURES:
[brams castle.details[1]] -> - Wraith's Gown
[brams castle.details[3]] -> Bram's Castle is more of a home and
[brams castle.details[4]] -> less of a fortress. While his servants
[brams castle.details[5]] -> will put up a fight, adventurers will
[brams castle.details[6]] -> have the opportunity to manage each
[brams castle.details[7]] -> room, eventually facing the vampire
[brams castle.details[8]] -> at the top of the castle.
[brams castle.details[10]] -> Take care not to let the tight halls
[brams castle.details[11]] -> overwhelm you. Be warned that the
[brams castle.details[12]] -> upper floors are off-limits to many
[brams castle.details[13]] -> bestial followers.
[breakable barriers.blurb[0]] -> Some barriers may appear impassable
[breakable barriers.blurb[1]] -> at first, but their integrity is such
[breakable barriers.blurb[2]] -> that a few strong hits can break
[breakable barriers.blurb[3]] -> open the way. Depending on the material,
[breakable barriers.blurb[4]] -> they have different weaknesses.
[breakable barriers.details[0]] -> BARRIER TYPES:
[breakable barriers.details[1]] -> - Wood
[breakable barriers.details[2]] ->    Flammable, takes extra damage
[breakable barriers.details[3]] ->    from axes and unarmed attacks.
[breakable barriers.details[4]] -> - Brick & Stone
[breakable barriers.details[5]] ->    Takes extra damage from maces.
[breakable barriers.details[6]] -> - Cordage (webs and thicket)
[breakable barriers.details[7]] ->    Flammable, takes extra damage
[breakable barriers.details[8]] ->    from axes and swords.
[breakable barriers.details[10]] -> All breakable barrier types take
[breakable barriers.details[11]] -> full damage from force, lightning
[breakable barriers.details[12]] -> and fire spell attacks, but they
[breakable barriers.details[13]] -> are immune to cold.
[brimstone boulder.blurb[0]] -> Boulders are threatening enough,
[brimstone boulder.blurb[1]] -> but veins of brimstone allow this
[brimstone boulder.blurb[2]] -> hellish variety to roll over lava.
[brimstone boulder.blurb[3]] -> They'll also detonate in a
[brimstone boulder.blurb[4]] -> fiery explosion on contact.
[brimstone boulder.blurb[5]] -> AVOID.
[brimstone boulder.details[0]] -> Summoning brimstone boulders is
[brimstone boulder.details[1]] -> a power unique to Baphomet, dealing
[brimstone boulder.details[2]] -> 50 damage regardless of the victim's
[brimstone boulder.details[3]] -> armor or constitution.
[brimstone boulder.details[5]] -> Upon impact, brimstone boulders
[brimstone boulder.details[6]] -> explode into a column of flames
[brimstone boulder.details[7]] -> dealing additional magic damage.
[brimstone boulder.details[9]] -> On the molten throne, these give
[brimstone boulder.details[10]] -> Baphomet a particular edge, as the
[brimstone boulder.details[11]] -> pools of lava he uses to traverse
[brimstone boulder.details[12]] -> are no longer shelters from the
[brimstone boulder.details[13]] -> rolling destruction.
[brimstone boulder.details[15]] -> An adventurer who levitates can
[brimstone boulder.details[16]] -> still nonetheless avoid the boulders,
[brimstone boulder.details[17]] -> while they continue to crush through
[brimstone boulder.details[18]] -> the very minions he has summoned.
[ceiling trap.blurb[0]] -> By tapping directly into magical energy
[ceiling trap.blurb[1]] -> from the crystal-dense ceilings, these
[ceiling trap.blurb[2]] -> security systems can hinder invaders
[ceiling trap.blurb[3]] -> with almost no maintenance cost.
[ceiling trap.blurb[5]] -> An innovation available in several varieties.
[ceiling trap.details[0]] -> CEILING TRAP TYPES:
[ceiling trap.details[1]] -> - Forcebolt
[ceiling trap.details[2]] -> - Cold
[ceiling trap.details[3]] -> - Fireball
[ceiling trap.details[4]] -> - Lightning
[ceiling trap.details[5]] -> - Magic Missile
[ceiling trap.details[6]] -> - Sleep
[ceiling trap.details[7]] -> - Slow
[ceiling trap.details[8]] -> - Confuse
[ceiling trap.details[10]] -> Though simliar to magic traps, the
[ceiling trap.details[11]] -> ceiling trap can't be destroyed.
[ceiling trap.details[13]] -> Dropped items can fool the trap, but it
[ceiling trap.details[14]] -> will fire continuously. Time between
[ceiling trap.details[15]] -> each spell permits dodging through.
[chest.blurb[0]] -> CHESTS may hold valuable treasures that
[chest.blurb[1]] -> will aid adventurers. Equipment within
[chest.blurb[2]] -> is never cursed. Unfortunately, before
[chest.blurb[3]] -> opening, chests are indistinguishable
[chest.blurb[4]] -> from mimics.
[chest.details[0]] -> CHEST TYPES:
[chest.details[1]] -> - 13.5% Weaponry and Armor
[chest.details[2]] -> - 13.5% Scrolls and Magic Supplies
[chest.details[3]] -> - 13.5% Potions and Alchemy Supplies
[chest.details[4]] -> - 13.5% Tools and Tinkering Supplies
[chest.details[5]] -> - 13.5% Jewels and Enchanted Jewelry
[chest.details[6]] -> - 13.5% Foodstuffs
[chest.details[7]] -> - 13.5% Random Items
[chest.details[8]] -> - 5.5% Empty/Garbage
[chest.details[10]] -> Items found inside chests are usually
[chest.details[11]] -> of a higher quality than those found
[chest.details[12]] -> scattered along the dungeon floors,
[chest.details[13]] -> often uncursed.
[chest.details[15]] -> Chests usually have a 10% chance of
[chest.details[16]] -> of being locked and a 5% chance of
[chest.details[17]] -> being mimics.
[chest.details[19]] -> When unlocked with tinkering skill
[chest.details[20]] -> using a lockpick, a chest's locking
[chest.details[21]] -> mechanism is salvaged, yielding
[chest.details[22]] -> magic and metal scrap in the chest.
[citadel sanctum.blurb[0]] -> In the core of the Citadel, its nature
[citadel sanctum.blurb[1]] -> is revealed as a gigantic magical device,
[citadel sanctum.blurb[2]] -> created to open up rifts to another
[citadel sanctum.blurb[3]] -> dimension with forbidden magic.
[citadel sanctum.blurb[5]] -> Its creators will protect it at all costs.
[citadel sanctum.details[0]] -> Orpheus and Erudyce had substantial
[citadel sanctum.details[1]] -> magical talent Herx never did when
[citadel sanctum.details[2]] -> he received the evil powers that
[citadel sanctum.details[3]] -> turned him into a lich.
[citadel sanctum.details[5]] -> Expect this pair to be far more
[citadel sanctum.details[6]] -> formidable with their spells in combat,
[citadel sanctum.details[7]] -> especially with their more recent
[citadel sanctum.details[8]] -> submission to evil magic.
[citadel sanctum.details[10]] -> Erudyce's cold spells will make it easier
[citadel sanctum.details[11]] -> for her brother to catch you in melee!
[citadel sanctum.details[13]] -> Each sibling will become enraged if
[citadel sanctum.details[14]] -> their counterpart is killed, enhancing
[citadel sanctum.details[15]] -> their combat prowess. Think ahead!
[cockatrice lair.blurb[0]] -> While no symbiosis between these scaly
[cockatrice lair.blurb[1]] -> creatures is known, Cockatrices and
[cockatrice lair.blurb[2]] -> Kobolds are historically depicted
[cockatrice lair.blurb[3]] -> together by Kobold tribal art. It is
[cockatrice lair.blurb[4]] -> thought they worship the beasts.
[cockatrice lair.details[0]] -> SECRET LEVEL TREASURES:
[cockatrice lair.details[1]] -> - Dragon's Mail
[cockatrice lair.details[3]] -> This fiercely guarded kobold maze
[cockatrice lair.details[4]] -> is the greatest known example of
[cockatrice lair.details[5]] -> their ingenuity and culture.
[cockatrice lair.details[7]] -> Frought with traps and puzzles,
[cockatrice lair.details[8]] -> this lair is designed to keep intruders
[cockatrice lair.details[9]] -> out.
[cockatrice lair.details[11]] -> Strong enchantments prevent
[cockatrice lair.details[12]] -> teleporting, dig, open, and levitation.
[cockatrice lair.details[13]] -> Those seeking treasure must navigate
[cockatrice lair.details[14]] -> these tunnels the hard way, and hope
[cockatrice lair.details[15]] -> they can escape.
[containers.blurb[0]] -> Dungeon denizens often gather
[containers.blurb[1]] -> belongings into containers or
[containers.blurb[2]] -> hide them away in sheltered spots.
[containers.blurb[4]] -> Gold and items may be found when
[containers.blurb[5]] -> bashing fragile objects open.
[containers.details[0]] -> The contents of a breakable container
[containers.details[1]] -> varies greatly depending on where it's
[containers.details[2]] -> found.
[containers.details[4]] -> What remains most consistent is a
[containers.details[5]] -> handful of coins, or a random item
[containers.details[6]] -> squirreled away.
[containers.details[8]] -> Rarely, a small creature, or even a
[containers.details[9]] -> small group may be tucked inside for
[containers.details[10]] -> shelter.
[crystal caves.blurb[0]] -> While this rich source of extremely
[crystal caves.blurb[1]] -> rare crystal was only recently discovered,
[crystal caves.blurb[2]] -> the Magicians' Guild archmagisters
[crystal caves.blurb[3]] -> quickly sealed it off, for Hamlet's
[crystal caves.blurb[4]] -> safety, of course.
[crystal caves.details[0]] -> INHABITANTS:
[crystal caves.details[1]] -> Kobolds, Scarabs, Insectoids,
[crystal caves.details[2]] -> Automatons, Incubi, Crystal Golems,
[crystal caves.details[3]] -> Cockatrices
[crystal caves.details[5]] -> NEW TRAP:
[crystal caves.details[6]] -> Ceiling Trap
[crystal caves.details[8]] -> The crystal within these caves gives
[crystal caves.details[9]] -> many of its denizens intense power
[crystal caves.details[10]] -> beyond what is naturally possible.
[crystal caves.details[12]] -> Confident adventurers coming from
[crystal caves.details[13]] -> the ruins would be wise to exercise
[crystal caves.details[14]] -> greater caution with new foes.
[daedalus.blurb[0]] -> Closely bound to the minotaur,
[daedalus.blurb[1]] -> DAEDALUS SHRINES seem to always be
[daedalus.blurb[2]] -> nearby when the minotaur is on the hunt.
[daedalus.blurb[4]] -> Savvy adventurers can touch them to
[daedalus.blurb[5]] -> reveal hope for a speedy escape.
[daedalus.details[0]] -> These shrines turn to point to the
[daedalus.details[1]] -> primary exit when touched, sending a
[daedalus.details[2]] -> divining beam forth in that direction.
[daedalus.details[3]] -> This also reveals the map between the
[daedalus.details[4]] -> shrine and the exit!
[daedalus.details[6]] -> If activated within 30 seconds before
[daedalus.details[7]] -> the minotaur's arrival, the shrine
[daedalus.details[8]] -> boosts the user's escape with an
[daedalus.details[9]] -> additional blessing of speed.
[daedalus.details[11]] -> Adventurers exploring together may
[daedalus.details[12]] -> find a bit more confidence splitting
[daedalus.details[13]] -> up where the minotaur is known to
[daedalus.details[14]] -> hunt, thanks to those who honor
[daedalus.details[15]] -> Daedalus.
[door.blurb[0]] -> It opens, it closes, and
[door.blurb[1]] -> may sometimes be locked!
[door.blurb[3]] -> Unlike the stubborn gate, DOORS can
[door.blurb[4]] -> be picked or bashed open. Monsters bash
[door.blurb[5]] -> through doors, if too dumb to open them.
[door.details[0]] -> While the lock spell can prevent
[door.details[1]] -> monsters from opening doors easily,
[door.details[2]] -> most don't have trouble bashing
[door.details[3]] -> through them anyway.
[door.details[4]] -> Doors are not a reliable way to keep
[door.details[5]] -> out monsters, even if locked.
[door.details[7]] -> Lockpicking a sealed door is usually
[door.details[8]] -> faster than bashing it, while providing
[door.details[9]] -> tinkering skill practice.
[door.details[11]] -> Doors take extra damage from axes
[door.details[12]] -> or unarmed strikes, if trained.
[door.details[13]] -> Damaging spells may also be effective.
[fountain.blurb[0]] -> FOUNTAIN waters refresh or apply magic
[fountain.blurb[1]] -> to an adventurer. They've also been known
[fountain.blurb[2]] -> to summon a succubus or incubus.
[fountain.blurb[4]] -> Magic doesn't come without peril.
[fountain.details[0]] -> FOUNTAIN USE POSSIBILITIES:
[fountain.details[1]] -> - 40% Apply a Random Potion Effect
[fountain.details[2]] -> - 30% Restore 5 HP, +Satiation
[fountain.details[3]] -> - 20% Summon Succubus/Incubus:
[fountain.details[4]] ->     Level 1-10:
[fountain.details[5]] ->         - Succubus (100%)
[fountain.details[6]] ->     Level 11-20/Underworld:
[fountain.details[7]] ->         - Succubus (50%)
[fountain.details[8]] ->         - Lesser Incubus (50%)
[fountain.details[9]] ->     Level 21+:
[fountain.details[10]] ->         - Incubus (100%)
[fountain.details[11]] -> - 7.5% Bless 1 Piece of Worn Equipment
[fountain.details[12]] -> - 2.5% Bless All Worn Equipment
[fountain.details[14]] -> Those skilled in alchemy avoid the
[fountain.details[15]] -> summoning of a foocubus when filling
[fountain.details[16]] -> a bottle with fountain liquids.
[fountain.details[18]] -> The otherworldly presence causes the
[fountain.details[19]] -> fountain to refill, allowing multiple
[fountain.details[20]] -> attempts to collect more potions.
[gnomish mines.blurb[0]] -> If the mines beneath Hamlet ever held
[gnomish mines.blurb[1]] -> gold, stories about it may've begun here.
[gnomish mines.blurb[3]] -> When a debt of gnomes descends on the hunt
[gnomish mines.blurb[4]] -> for riches, their greed cannot be satisfied.
[gnomish mines.details[0]] -> SECRET LEVEL TREASURES:
[gnomish mines.details[1]] -> - Sphinx's Casque
[gnomish mines.details[2]] -> - Dozens of gold veins to mine
[gnomish mines.details[4]] -> The greatest reward to be found
[gnomish mines.details[5]] -> here may be the experience earned
[gnomish mines.details[6]] -> by slaying so many gnomes!
[gnomish mines.details[8]] -> Lightning magicstaffs carried by
[gnomish mines.details[9]] -> gnomes are deadly, but proper
[gnomish mines.details[10]] -> ambushes can put the staffs in the
[gnomish mines.details[11]] -> hands of the adventurers, and turn
[gnomish mines.details[12]] -> the tides in their favor.
[gnomish mines.details[13]] -> Be sneaky to survive.
[gravestone.blurb[0]] -> Often chiseled with epitaphs, a GRAVE
[gravestone.blurb[1]] -> may result in a ghoul rising from the
[gravestone.blurb[2]] -> earth when disturbed. Some adventurers
[gravestone.blurb[3]] -> relish the opportunity to slay, or
[gravestone.blurb[4]] -> perhaps befriend, emergent undead.
[gravestone.details[0]] -> GRAVESTONE USE POSSIBILITIES:
[gravestone.details[1]] -> - 25% Disturb Ghoul
[gravestone.details[3]] ->         - Ghoul
[gravestone.details[4]] ->     Level 16+/Haunted Castle:
[gravestone.details[5]] ->         - Enslaved Ghoul
[gravestone.details[7]] -> If a ghoul is not disturbed by reading
[gravestone.details[8]] -> the gravestone's epitaph, it otherwise
[gravestone.details[9]] -> only acts as an obstacle.
[gravestone.details[11]] -> If a trap or puzzle activates a
[gravestone.details[12]] -> gravestone, it will always produce
[gravestone.details[13]] -> an undead ghoul.
[hall of trials.blurb[0]] -> Founded by unaffiliated adventurers,
[hall of trials.blurb[1]] -> the HALL OF TRIALS was established shortly
[hall of trials.blurb[2]] -> after Herx's imprisonment in the Devils'
[hall of trials.blurb[3]] -> Bastion. Nobody knows what became of
[hall of trials.blurb[4]] -> its benefactors.
[hall of trials.details[0]] -> While some adventurers seek to earn
[hall of trials.details[1]] -> diplomas from the Hall of Trials all
[hall of trials.details[2]] -> at once, many prefer to revisit the
[hall of trials.details[3]] -> mysterious academy from time to time,
[hall of trials.details[4]] -> mastering disciplines gradually.
[hall of trials.details[6]] -> The greatest thing to be gained here
[hall of trials.details[7]] -> is knowledge. Student awards can
[hall of trials.details[8]] -> open more learning opportunities.
[hall of trials.details[10]] -> While no single guild built it,
[hall of trials.details[11]] -> the Hall of Trials is the first effort
[hall of trials.details[12]] -> of the movement of united guilds,
[hall of trials.details[13]] -> whose objective is to defeat chaos.
[hamlet.blurb[0]] -> The reclaimed HAMLET has been
[hamlet.blurb[1]] -> hastily renovated by the recently
[hamlet.blurb[2]] -> freed prisoners of the mines.
[hamlet.blurb[4]] -> In this district nearest the Minehead,
[hamlet.blurb[5]] -> the Magicians' Guild holds high prominence.
[hamlet.details[0]] -> Friendly heroes have unparalleled
[hamlet.details[1]] -> access to these kinds of Hamlet shops:
[hamlet.details[2]] -> - 2x Arms & Armor
[hamlet.details[3]] -> - General Store
[hamlet.details[4]] -> - Jeweler
[hamlet.details[5]] -> - Magicstaff
[hamlet.details[6]] -> - Bookstore
[hamlet.details[7]] -> - Alchemist
[hamlet.details[8]] -> - Delicatessen
[hamlet.details[10]] -> Monsters traveling to Hamlet will be
[hamlet.details[11]] -> attacked on sight. The inn bunkroom
[hamlet.details[12]] -> conveniently hosts a sewer entrance,
[hamlet.details[13]] -> through which one can travel safely
[hamlet.details[14]] -> to the back of the Magicians' Guild.
[hamlet.details[16]] -> Hidden below, there are polymorph
[hamlet.details[17]] -> potions, allowing them to shop freely.
[haunted castle.blurb[0]] -> Before he was sealed away, the citizens
[haunted castle.blurb[1]] -> of Hamlet were enslaved by the Baron
[haunted castle.blurb[2]] -> to build this CASTLE for him to occupy.
[haunted castle.blurb[4]] -> The walls were formed by stone
[haunted castle.blurb[5]] -> excavated by the miners.
[haunted castle.details[0]] -> SECRET LEVEL TREASURES:
[haunted castle.details[1]] -> - Oracle's Treads
[haunted castle.details[2]] -> - Hidden treasure chests
[haunted castle.details[3]] -> - 4 Potions of levitation
[haunted castle.details[5]] -> Ghouls here are cursed to defend
[haunted castle.details[6]] -> the Baron's possessions, and rise when
[haunted castle.details[7]] -> his things are disturbed. Prior to
[haunted castle.details[8]] -> looting, plan the escape or defense!
[haunted castle.details[10]] -> Secret treasure chests are
[haunted castle.details[11]] -> hidden behind a waterfall.
[haunted castle.details[12]] -> Explore the castle towers thoroughly
[haunted castle.details[13]] -> and find how to reveal the way.
[hell.blurb[0]] -> A dimension crafted for human suffering,
[hell.blurb[1]] -> but also home to many magical beasts
[hell.blurb[2]] -> and monsters.
[hell.blurb[4]] -> Here vile devils seek ways to dominate
[hell.blurb[5]] -> the realms of mortals and immortals alike.
[hell.details[0]] -> INHABITANTS:
[hell.details[1]] -> Succubi, Incubi, Imps, Demons,
[hell.details[2]] -> Shadows, Goatmen
[hell.details[4]] -> NEW TRAP:
[hell.details[5]] -> Summoning Trap
[hell.details[7]] -> Few survive Hell for long.
[hell.details[8]] -> Dodge spells with swift feet while
[hell.details[9]] -> watching for spike traps. Arrows traps
[hell.details[10]] -> might push adventurers into lava!
[hell.details[12]] -> To survive one must think quickly.
[hell.details[13]] -> Cure ailment will aleviate burning.
[herx lair.blurb[0]] -> The ancient ruins descend into a place
[herx lair.blurb[1]] -> that channels the flow of primordial power.
[herx lair.blurb[3]] -> Those with the will to control it can
[herx lair.blurb[4]] -> exert their influence here, as the
[herx lair.blurb[5]] -> veil between realms is thin.
[herx lair.details[0]] -> If an adventurer brings mystic orbs
[herx lair.details[1]] -> to this place, they can be placed on
[herx lair.details[2]] -> pedestals in the northern rooms:
[herx lair.details[3]] -> - Green Orb improves DEX and PER
[herx lair.details[4]] -> - Red Orb improves STR and CON
[herx lair.details[5]] -> - Blue Orb improves INT and Magic
[herx lair.details[6]] ->     Resistance
[herx lair.details[8]] -> Herx waits to surprise his foes
[herx lair.details[9]] -> until they are approaching the
[herx lair.details[10]] -> middle of his arena. Keep allies
[herx lair.details[11]] -> on the outer edge of the room and
[herx lair.details[12]] -> give yourself time to prepare.
[herx lair.details[13]] -> Magic Reflection is recommended.
[hunters guild.blurb[0]] -> Founded by simple pioneers,
[hunters guild.blurb[1]] -> the HUNTERS' GUILD now employs Rogues,
[hunters guild.blurb[2]] -> Hunters, and Ninjas who are capable of
[hunters guild.blurb[3]] -> snuffing out terrifying threats with
[hunters guild.blurb[4]] -> well-organized efficiency.
[hunters guild.details[0]] -> Members of the hunters' guild rely on
[hunters guild.details[1]] -> ambushing to do their good work. They
[hunters guild.details[2]] -> regard this as the least costly,
[hunters guild.details[3]] -> the least risky, and thus the most
[hunters guild.details[4]] -> moral method to serve civilization.
[hunters guild.details[6]] -> Members offer death as their first
[hunters guild.details[7]] -> solution. This has earned them a
[hunters guild.details[8]] -> reputation as death worshippers.
[hunters guild.details[10]] -> In their own words:
[hunters guild.details[11]] ->    Death is necessary for life.
[hunters guild.details[12]] ->    Our duty is to choose the
[hunters guild.details[13]] ->    right recipients for each.
[labyrinth.blurb[0]] -> Geomancers theorize that the waters
[labyrinth.blurb[1]] -> of the Swamps once burbled up from
[labyrinth.blurb[2]] -> a massive subterranean ocean.
[labyrinth.blurb[4]] -> However, miners found only dry sand
[labyrinth.blurb[5]] -> and ruins in the depths below.
[labyrinth.details[0]] -> INHABITANTS:
[labyrinth.details[1]] -> Scarabs, Scorpions, Lesser Insectoids,
[labyrinth.details[2]] -> Goblins, Trolls
[labyrinth.details[4]] -> NEW TRAP:
[labyrinth.details[5]] -> Spike Trap
[labyrinth.details[7]] -> With large, winding mazes, the
[labyrinth.details[8]] -> labyrinths are quite deadly when
[labyrinth.details[9]] -> paired with two threats:
[labyrinth.details[10]] -> Starvation and minotaurs.
[labyrinth.details[11]] -> Magic mapping can help with speedy
[labyrinth.details[12]] -> exploration. Bring a method for
[labyrinth.details[13]] -> digging to open hidden paths.
[lava.blurb[0]] -> It's liquid-hot magma!
[lava.blurb[2]] -> Anything that falls in is
[lava.blurb[3]] -> engulfed in flame and destroyed,
[lava.blurb[4]] -> including clumsy adventurers.
[lava.details[0]] -> Lava is a deadly obstacle with
[lava.details[1]] -> little reason to attempt swimming in
[lava.details[2]] -> it, setting ablaze whatever enters.
[lava.details[4]] -> Automatons who really want to
[lava.details[5]] -> increase their temperature might
[lava.details[6]] -> find a short dip to be useful - in spite
[lava.details[7]] -> of the rapid damage that lava causes.
[lava.details[9]] -> Waterwalking allows adventurers
[lava.details[10]] -> and their followers to avoid sinking
[lava.details[11]] -> into the surface of lava.
[lava.details[13]] -> Should've called it liquidwalking.
[lever.blurb[0]] -> LEVERS are reliable tools
[lever.blurb[1]] -> for a dungeon architect.
[lever.blurb[3]] -> Using hidden mechanisms, the power of
[lever.blurb[4]] -> leverage can activate anything from traps
[lever.blurb[5]] -> to doorways and even mystical gadgets.
[lever.details[0]] -> Some levers have a timed effect,
[lever.details[1]] -> requiring them to be cranked up
[lever.details[2]] -> multiple times before activating.
[lever.details[3]] -> Often these are attached to a
[lever.details[4]] -> challenge which demands speed.
[lever.details[6]] -> Sometimes lever mechanisms overlap
[lever.details[7]] -> with hidden machinery attached to
[lever.details[8]] -> other dungeon traps. These overlaps
[lever.details[9]] -> can be confusing but may also provide
[lever.details[10]] -> emergent behaviors to exploit.
[lever.details[12]] -> Player ghosts can pull levers, allowing
[lever.details[13]] -> some challenges to be cheated.
[magic trap.blurb[0]] -> These magical pylons once acted
[magic trap.blurb[1]] -> as channels of magic for those
[magic trap.blurb[2]] -> who lived here to use.
[magic trap.blurb[4]] -> They have since been corrupted
[magic trap.blurb[5]] -> into beacons of chaos.
[magic trap.details[0]] -> MAGIC TRAP TYPES:
[magic trap.details[1]] -> - Forcebolt
[magic trap.details[2]] -> - Cold
[magic trap.details[3]] -> - Fireball
[magic trap.details[4]] -> - Lightning
[magic trap.details[5]] -> - Magic Missile
[magic trap.details[6]] -> - Sleep
[magic trap.details[7]] -> - Slow
[magic trap.details[8]] -> - Confuse
[magic trap.details[10]] -> Some adventurers have the means to
[magic trap.details[11]] -> dig these traps to break them, which
[magic trap.details[12]] -> can greatly simplify exploration.
[magic trap.details[13]] -> If guiding followers, avoid confusion
[magic trap.details[14]] -> traps! Cure ailment saves friendships.
[magicians guild.blurb[0]] -> Fostering innovation and ambition, the
[magicians guild.blurb[1]] -> MAGICIANS' GUILD trains Arcanists,
[magicians guild.blurb[2]] -> Healers, and Wizards.
[magicians guild.blurb[4]] -> A paradoxical source of time-honored
[magicians guild.blurb[5]] -> wisdom and ill-conceived revolution.
[magicians guild.details[0]] -> Agents of the magicians' guild are
[magicians guild.details[1]] -> adaptable spellcasters, able to
[magicians guild.details[2]] -> read and memorize most spells, as
[magicians guild.details[3]] -> long as they have been practicing.
[magicians guild.details[5]] -> Most magicians have secondary skills
[magicians guild.details[6]] -> which allow them to reserve magic for
[magicians guild.details[7]] -> when a spell is truly necessary.
[magicians guild.details[9]] -> They follow a complex philosophy of
[magicians guild.details[10]] -> the makeup of the universe, pondering
[magicians guild.details[11]] -> how each element combines to account
[magicians guild.details[12]] -> for material reality, the spirit realm,
[magicians guild.details[13]] -> as well as human virtues and vices.
[masons guild.blurb[0]] -> Originally a guild of stoneworkers, the
[masons guild.blurb[1]] -> Masons' Guild's role in communities now
[masons guild.blurb[2]] -> includes all manner of work that
[masons guild.blurb[3]] -> requires organized use of might.
[masons guild.blurb[4]] -> Barbarians, Warriors, and Wanderers
[masons guild.blurb[5]] -> often place membership.
[masons guild.details[0]] -> A proud organization of workers
[masons guild.details[1]] -> and soldiers who are certain that
[masons guild.details[2]] -> they're the foundation of
[masons guild.details[3]] -> civilization itself.
[masons guild.details[5]] -> While other guilds may disagree
[masons guild.details[6]] -> on that point, none deny that their
[masons guild.details[7]] -> mighty arms and strong backs are to
[masons guild.details[8]] -> thank for the settlement and
[masons guild.details[9]] -> fortification of all great cities.
[masons guild.details[11]] -> Members of the masons' guild believe
[masons guild.details[12]] -> in their duty to protect peace and
[masons guild.details[13]] -> build new, fruitful futures.
[merchants guild.blurb[0]] -> An organization of Merchants, Mechanists,
[merchants guild.blurb[1]] -> and Brewers, the MERCHANTS' GUILD is
[merchants guild.blurb[2]] -> quietly respected as the most
[merchants guild.blurb[3]] -> powerful guild in the realm.
[merchants guild.blurb[5]] -> Some say Herx was a member long ago.
[merchants guild.details[0]] -> Merchants' guild members are defined
[merchants guild.details[1]] -> by their resourcefulness. While often
[merchants guild.details[2]] -> lacking in might or arcane talent, they
[merchants guild.details[3]] -> rely on found items more than others.
[merchants guild.details[5]] -> The guild shepherds associates to
[merchants guild.details[6]] -> identify and exploit tools they have
[merchants guild.details[7]] -> at their disposal to ensure success.
[merchants guild.details[9]] -> In parties, merchants' guild sponsored
[merchants guild.details[10]] -> classes are able to discover solutions
[merchants guild.details[11]] -> that traditional adventurers don't
[merchants guild.details[12]] -> often consider. Adaptability is key.
[minehead.blurb[0]] -> Just through the ruins of Hamlet
[minehead.blurb[1]] -> lies the MINEHEAD where citizens
[minehead.blurb[2]] -> slaved away for the Baron.
[minehead.blurb[4]] -> Entering this place is a one-way trip unless
[minehead.blurb[5]] -> the curse on Hamlet can be broken.
[minehead.details[0]] -> Many adventuring parties camp here
[minehead.details[1]] -> as they prepare for their attempt at
[minehead.details[2]] -> lifting the Baron's curse.
[minehead.details[4]] -> A convenient location to plan and
[minehead.details[5]] -> trade equipment or food, preparing
[minehead.details[6]] -> for the dangerous path ahead.
[minehead.details[8]] -> Allied spellcasters can benefit from
[minehead.details[9]] -> sharing spellbooks. As long as they
[minehead.details[10]] -> have the durability, memorizing each
[minehead.details[11]] -> others' spellbooks multiplies their
[minehead.details[12]] -> benefit to a party.
[mines.blurb[0]] -> Initially mined for iron, and later scoured
[mines.blurb[1]] -> in a fruitless search for gold, the MINES
[mines.blurb[2]] -> became the home of Baron Herx's
[mines.blurb[3]] -> mercenary army as they imprisoned the
[mines.blurb[4]] -> Hamlet miners.
[mines.details[0]] -> INHABITANTS:
[mines.details[1]] -> Rats, Skeletons, Spiders, Trolls,
[mines.details[2]] -> Humans
[mines.details[4]] -> NEW TRAP:
[mines.details[5]] -> Boulder Trap
[mines.details[7]] -> The mines will test your basic
[mines.details[8]] -> dungeoning skills, including ambushes,
[mines.details[9]] -> blocking, keeping an eye out for traps
[mines.details[10]] -> and managing your food supply.
[mines.details[12]] -> Avoid fights you can't win, and learn
[mines.details[13]] -> enemy weaknesses to shorten fights.
[minetown.blurb[0]] -> A place of respite within the Mines,
[minetown.blurb[1]] -> hidden from Herx's army. Thought to be
[minetown.blurb[2]] -> a myth by Hamlet miners, history doesn't
[minetown.blurb[3]] -> say if the hopeful people built MINETOWN,
[minetown.blurb[4]] -> or if they discovered it.
[minetown.details[0]] -> SECRET LEVEL TREASURES:
[minetown.details[1]] -> - Four random shops
[minetown.details[2]] -> - Four treasure chests
[minetown.details[3]] -> - Several humans to recruit
[minetown.details[5]] -> Accessing the hidden treasures in
[minetown.details[6]] -> Minetown requires a way to get past
[minetown.details[7]] -> the gates which guard the lake.
[minetown.details[8]] -> Open, dig, pickaxes or even teleport
[minetown.details[9]] -> may do the job.
[minetown.details[11]] -> Four shops means four shopkeepers.
[minetown.details[12]] -> Minetown can be dangerous to visit
[minetown.details[13]] -> for ill-prepared monsters.
[minotaur maze.blurb[0]] -> Myths tell of a maze that hides
[minotaur maze.blurb[1]] -> artifacts of unmatched power.
[minotaur maze.blurb[3]] -> The high walls and broad hallways are
[minotaur maze.blurb[4]] -> perfectly sized for a terrifyingly large
[minotaur maze.blurb[5]] -> protector who would guard such treasure.
[minotaur maze.details[0]] -> SECRET LEVEL TREASURES:
[minotaur maze.details[3]] -> Look for nearby gatehouse levers if
[minotaur maze.details[4]] -> closed gates block the way. A spell
[minotaur maze.details[5]] -> of opening, or digging, can help!
[minotaur maze.details[7]] -> The silver key at the start of the
[minotaur maze.details[8]] -> maze gives access to Gungnir in the
[minotaur maze.details[9]] -> center. But the key may be useful if
[minotaur maze.details[10]] -> you don't have need of the spear!
[molten throne.blurb[0]] -> The seat of Baphomet's power.
[molten throne.blurb[1]] -> This devil has chosen a location where
[molten throne.blurb[2]] -> magic may flow more easily to the mortal
[molten throne.blurb[3]] -> realm, allowing his influence to seep in.
[molten throne.blurb[5]] -> Other realms may similarly be close by.
[molten throne.details[0]] -> While Baphomet is a being of great
[molten throne.details[1]] -> power, an adventurer invading his
[molten throne.details[2]] -> realm is not what he expects. Herx
[molten throne.details[3]] -> is his intended puppet with whom he
[molten throne.details[4]] -> sought to corrupt the mortal world.
[molten throne.details[6]] -> Regardless, even caught unprepared,
[molten throne.details[7]] -> his mastery of fiery brimstone with
[molten throne.details[8]] -> the command of evil demons and spirits
[molten throne.details[9]] -> guarantee he won't submit easily.
[molten throne.details[11]] -> If he is defeated, beware of rival
[molten throne.details[12]] -> devils sending minotaur agents to
[molten throne.details[13]] -> claim his throne for themselves.
[murky water.blurb[0]] -> Most denizens are careful not to
[murky water.blurb[1]] -> enter foul pools of dungeon water.
[murky water.blurb[3]] -> Filled with dense rot, just about
[murky water.blurb[4]] -> anything will float on it, including
[murky water.blurb[5]] -> adventurers with places to go.
[murky water.details[0]] -> While murky water is usually a trivial
[murky water.details[1]] -> obstacle, adventurers should avoid
[murky water.details[2]] -> combat while swimming.
[murky water.details[4]] -> An amulet of olympic swimming can
[murky water.details[5]] -> all but eliminate the inconvenience
[murky water.details[6]] -> of having to swim, and can save lives
[murky water.details[7]] -> if a hasty swimming escape is needed.
[murky water.details[9]] -> Water will put out fires, and washes
[murky water.details[10]] -> away the effects of polymorph.
[murky water.details[11]] -> Monsters should make sure their
[murky water.details[12]] -> shopping is done before falling in.
[mystic library.blurb[0]] -> The Magicians' Guild still
[mystic library.blurb[1]] -> holds a strange connection to
[mystic library.blurb[2]] -> the MYSTIC LIBRARY, a pocket dimension
[mystic library.blurb[3]] -> accessible by magic from the ruins
[mystic library.blurb[4]] -> buried deep beneath Hamlet.
[mystic library.details[0]] -> SECRET LEVEL TREASURES:
[mystic library.details[1]] -> - Chests of random magic items
[mystic library.details[2]] -> - Several humans to recruit
[mystic library.details[4]] -> The library is filled with rewards
[mystic library.details[5]] -> for friendly adventurers. Use dig and
[mystic library.details[6]] -> levitate to explore for hidden chests.
[mystic library.details[8]] -> Caches of scrolls, spellbooks, and
[mystic library.details[9]] -> magicstaffs can help late-blooming
[mystic library.details[10]] -> magic-users to mature their craft.
[mystic library.details[11]] -> Non-magic users can still benefit
[mystic library.details[12]] -> from many of the scrolls.
[obelisk.blurb[0]] -> The shapeless void of the Underworld
[obelisk.blurb[1]] -> can be confusing to traverse.
[obelisk.blurb[3]] -> These shrines seize upon hapless spirits
[obelisk.blurb[4]] -> when touched, carrying them off to
[obelisk.blurb[5]] -> another part of the realm.
[obelisk.details[0]] -> While initially random, obelisks lead
[obelisk.details[1]] -> to each room in sequence, eventually
[obelisk.details[2]] -> looping back around to the start.
[obelisk.details[4]] -> This does enable exploration of the
[obelisk.details[5]] -> underworld's sea of pits, but also
[obelisk.details[6]] -> sends adventurers along with no
[obelisk.details[7]] -> no warning of what awaits them on the
[obelisk.details[8]] -> other side.
[obelisk.details[10]] -> Some adventurers ready potions,
[obelisk.details[11]] -> stealth, or a raised shield. Others
[obelisk.details[12]] -> send a follower through first, waiting
[obelisk.details[13]] -> to see if they survive the journey.
[pits.blurb[0]] -> Ambling denizens are wise enough
[pits.blurb[1]] -> not to fling themselves into the
[pits.blurb[2]] -> vast emptiness of PITS.
[pits.blurb[3]] -> Those who defy gravity should make
[pits.blurb[4]] -> sure to land on solid ground,
[pits.blurb[5]] -> or face certain death.
[pits.details[0]] -> Pits often taunt adventurers with
[pits.details[1]] -> unreachable treasures on the other
[pits.details[2]] -> side.
[pits.details[4]] -> While levitation is a great
[pits.details[5]] -> solution, often one might also find
[pits.details[6]] -> access by digging through walls or
[pits.details[7]] -> opening gates on the other side.
[pits.details[9]] -> Adventuring parties may find pits
[pits.details[10]] -> to be a convenient way to dispose of
[pits.details[11]] -> unwanted items, making sure allies
[pits.details[12]] -> don't waste time picking through
[pits.details[13]] -> piles of cursed junk.
[portcullis.blurb[0]] -> A portcullis that can only be
[portcullis.blurb[1]] -> passed by raising its iron bars.
[portcullis.blurb[3]] -> Most often, a nearby lever will operate it,
[portcullis.blurb[4]] -> though crafty magic may also do the job.
[portcullis.details[0]] -> Not all gates have a lever that
[portcullis.details[1]] -> operates them. A spell of opening
[portcullis.details[2]] -> will allow adventurers to bypass
[portcullis.details[3]] -> many dungeon challenges and traps.
[portcullis.details[5]] -> Since only the minotaur can shatter
[portcullis.details[6]] -> gates, using a lever to close an open
[portcullis.details[7]] -> gate is a very reliable way to keep
[portcullis.details[8]] -> monsters away if you need a moment.
[portcullis.details[10]] -> Some gates are held closed by a
[portcullis.details[11]] -> mechanism, rather than being held
[portcullis.details[12]] -> open by one. These gates cannot be
[portcullis.details[13]] -> opened with magic.
[ruins.blurb[0]] -> No one knows which ancient tribe
[ruins.blurb[1]] -> built these enchanted RUINS.
[ruins.blurb[3]] -> Legends tell of a magical catastrophe that
[ruins.blurb[4]] -> once sent an entire city to the underworld
[ruins.blurb[5]] -> forever. Perhaps this is that place.
[ruins.details[0]] -> INHABITANTS:
[ruins.details[1]] -> Demons, Gnomes, Young Vampires,
[ruins.details[2]] -> Bugbears, Damaged Automatons
[ruins.details[4]] -> NEW TRAP:
[ruins.details[5]] -> Magic Trap
[ruins.details[7]] -> The ruins' open spaces are far easier
[ruins.details[8]] -> to navigate than the labyrinths, but
[ruins.details[9]] -> the threats may come from anywhere.
[ruins.details[10]] -> Situational awareness and decisive
[ruins.details[11]] -> damage are essential for success.
[ruins.details[13]] -> Traverse pits to discover secrets.
[shop.blurb[0]] -> SHOPS are recognizable no
[shop.blurb[1]] -> matter where they're found.
[shop.blurb[3]] -> Even monsters know not to threaten
[shop.blurb[4]] -> shopkeepers, but they won't mind if you
[shop.blurb[5]] -> rummage through their chests for freebies.
[shop.details[0]] -> SHOP TYPES:
[shop.details[1]] -> - Arms & Armor
[shop.details[2]] -> - Hats
[shop.details[3]] -> - Hunting Supply
[shop.details[4]] -> - Delicatessen
[shop.details[5]] -> - Alchemist
[shop.details[6]] -> - Hardware Store
[shop.details[7]] -> - Magicstaffs
[shop.details[8]] -> - Bookstore
[shop.details[9]] -> - Jeweler
[shop.details[10]] -> - General Store
[shop.details[12]] -> Each shop has a sign signifying
[shop.details[13]] -> the kind of wares it trades in.
[shop.details[14]] -> Only general stores buy all goods.
[shop.details[16]] -> Usually it's a good idea to spend!
[shop.details[17]] -> Shops may be rare, so taking the
[shop.details[18]] -> opportunity to buy supplies and earn
[shop.details[19]] -> trading skill is often a wise choice.
[shop.details[21]] -> With some trade skill, and charisma,
[shop.details[22]] -> shoppers can access a shop's private
[shop.details[23]] -> stock of consumables to help stay
[shop.details[24]] -> in good health and keep gear keen.
[shop.details[25]] -> A shop's private stock varies based on
[shop.details[26]] -> the shop type, often complementing the
[shop.details[27]] -> goods available for trade.
[shop.details[29]] -> Monsters, and adventurers marked
[shop.details[30]] -> with the WANTED status, are attacked
[shop.details[31]] -> on-sight by shopkeepers.
[shop.details[32]] -> Avoid collateral damage by making
[shop.details[33]] -> sure you are not between a
[shop.details[34]] -> shopkeeper and his target.
[sink.blurb[0]] -> SINK water may restore a little hunger,
[sink.blurb[1]] -> but the water can be scalding, slimes can
[sink.blurb[2]] -> hide in the pipes, and the plumbing
[sink.blurb[3]] -> quickly breaks.
[sink.blurb[5]] -> Use with empty bottles for best results.
[sink.details[0]] -> SINK USE POSSIBILITIES:
[sink.details[1]] -> - 60% Fresh Water
[sink.details[2]] -> - 20% Scalding Water
[sink.details[3]] -> - 10% Slime
[sink.details[4]] -> - 10% Find Ring
[sink.details[6]] -> Fresh sink water, served at the proper
[sink.details[7]] -> temperature, restores 1 HP. Those who
[sink.details[8]] -> have recently eaten a filling meal
[sink.details[9]] -> should take care when drinking from
[sink.details[10]] -> sinks so as not to be over-filled.
[sink.details[12]] -> If a slime emerges while tapping with
[sink.details[13]] -> an empty bottle, acid will be collected.
[sokoban.blurb[0]] -> Those who enter here say they feel
[sokoban.blurb[1]] -> watched and judged, as though they
[sokoban.blurb[2]] -> are being tested.
[sokoban.blurb[3]] -> Cynics claim it is a trick by cruel
[sokoban.blurb[4]] -> gods who enjoy watching mortals
[sokoban.blurb[5]] -> starve to death.
[sokoban.details[0]] -> SECRET LEVEL TREASURES:
[sokoban.details[1]] -> - Djinni's Brace
[sokoban.details[2]] -> - A fortune in gold pieces
[sokoban.details[4]] -> To solve this challenge, one must rid
[sokoban.details[5]] -> the room of all boulders using a ring
[sokoban.details[6]] -> of might or potion of strength.
[sokoban.details[8]] -> Pushing all boulders into pits is the
[sokoban.details[9]] -> path to victory, avoid letting them
[sokoban.details[10]] -> become stuck in corners - boulders
[sokoban.details[11]] -> cannot be pulled backward!
[sokoban.details[13]] -> Rewards will be reduced if boulders
[sokoban.details[14]] -> are destroyed to complete the puzzle.
[spike trap.blurb[0]] -> Somebody was either very cruel or
[spike trap.blurb[1]] -> terrified of something very large when
[spike trap.blurb[2]] -> they created these brutal devices.
[spike trap.blurb[4]] -> They are easy enough to spot and avoid...
[spike trap.blurb[5]] -> if you have time to watch your step.
[spike trap.details[0]] -> Spikes deal 50 damage, regardless
[spike trap.details[1]] -> of the victim's armor or constitution.
[spike trap.details[2]] -> Many spike traps trigger when walked
[spike trap.details[3]] -> on or over, regardless of levitation.
[spike trap.details[5]] -> Neutralize spikes by tossing
[spike trap.details[6]] -> an unwanted item on the trap, and
[spike trap.details[7]] -> they will not normally rearm until
[spike trap.details[8]] -> the item is removed. This will help
[spike trap.details[9]] -> followers survive as they wander.
[spike trap.details[11]] -> These traps are only dangerous when
[spike trap.details[12]] -> thrusting from below. Navigate
[spike trap.details[13]] -> through raised spikes to provide more
[spike trap.details[14]] -> time to maneuver certain challenges!
[summoning trap.blurb[0]] -> Empowered by arcane rituals the
[summoning trap.blurb[1]] -> SUMMONING TRAP can turn an empty room
[summoning trap.blurb[2]] -> into a deadly battlefield in an instant.
[summoning trap.blurb[4]] -> Take care when near these symbols.
[summoning trap.blurb[5]] -> They can be activated in many ways.
[summoning trap.details[0]] -> The symbol on the floor signals
[summoning trap.details[1]] -> the presence of this trap, but
[summoning trap.details[2]] -> drawing near, operating a lever,
[summoning trap.details[3]] -> or taking an offering from the floor
[summoning trap.details[4]] -> may all trigger the summoning.
[summoning trap.details[6]] -> Loud booms accompany activation
[summoning trap.details[7]] -> as demonic spirits transfer.
[summoning trap.details[9]] -> Some zealous adventurers like to
[summoning trap.details[10]] -> tempt summon traps, beckoning more
[summoning trap.details[11]] -> hellspawn to slay. But this is a risky
[summoning trap.details[12]] -> prospect, with little way of knowing
[summoning trap.details[13]] -> what kind of fight awaits.
[swamps.blurb[0]] -> Dense plants here were obliterated in the
[swamps.blurb[1]] -> effort to expand the Hamlet mines, but
[swamps.blurb[2]] -> the hydrophilic flora quickly recovered.
[swamps.blurb[4]] -> Sadly, the vegetation is known to
[swamps.blurb[5]] -> cause psychosis when eaten.
[swamps.details[0]] -> INHABITANTS:
[swamps.details[1]] -> Spiders, Goblins, Slimes, Ghouls, Trolls
[swamps.details[3]] -> NEW TRAP:
[swamps.details[4]] -> Arrow Trap
[swamps.details[6]] -> The swamps feature new threats
[swamps.details[7]] -> that attack at range. Stealth helps!
[swamps.details[9]] -> Beware goblins with magicstaffs.
[swamps.details[10]] -> Magic reflection is ideal if available.
[swamps.details[11]] -> Otherwise, ambush, or fight from afar
[swamps.details[12]] -> so you can dodge projectiles.
[swamps.details[13]] -> Dip into water to douse flames.
[temple.blurb[0]] -> An evil god has heard the prayers of
[temple.blurb[1]] -> swamp goblins and has provided a place
[temple.blurb[2]] -> on the surface for them to make blood
[temple.blurb[3]] -> sacrifices. A deadly path to this TEMPLE
[temple.blurb[4]] -> is provided for worship.
[temple.details[0]] -> SECRET LEVEL TREASURES:
[temple.details[1]] -> - 4 Potions of strength
[temple.details[2]] -> - A hoard of gold pieces
[temple.details[3]] -> - Several treasure chests
[temple.details[5]] -> Hidden rooms make use of a silver
[temple.details[6]] -> key, revealing more treasures.
[temple.details[7]] -> The Temple's traps may shut down
[temple.details[8]] -> access to secret areas if explorers
[temple.details[9]] -> are careless, or prisoners are freed.
[temple.details[11]] -> It is wise to take time to plan ahead
[temple.details[12]] -> to avoid blunders in the Temple.
[the church.blurb[0]] -> Officials of THE CHURCH play a passive
[the church.blurb[1]] -> cultural role until things get out of hand.
[the church.blurb[3]] -> Clerics, Monks, and Sextons act as
[the church.blurb[4]] -> agents of action when wrongs need
[the church.blurb[5]] -> to be made right.
[the church.details[0]] -> Members of the church see the events
[the church.details[1]] -> of the world as a tapestry of great
[the church.details[2]] -> purpose, and devote their lives seeking
[the church.details[3]] -> to understand and uphold it.
[the church.details[5]] -> With little ambition, officers usually
[the church.details[6]] -> withdraw from public affairs. But no
[the church.details[7]] -> other organization is so unified as the
[the church.details[8]] -> church when they find the course of
[the church.details[9]] -> history is straying from its purpose.
[the church.details[11]] -> Church agents tend to be practical,
[the church.details[12]] -> embracing physical and magic talents
[the church.details[13]] -> that provide uncomplicated utility.
[transition floor.blurb[0]] -> Each layer of the dungeons was once
[transition floor.blurb[1]] -> newly discovered, as miners dug deeper.
[transition floor.blurb[3]] -> Natural fissures formed between layers,
[transition floor.blurb[4]] -> requiring a bridge to be built, often
[transition floor.blurb[5]] -> taking weeks to finish.
[transition floor.details[0]] -> There is a strange sense of peace
[transition floor.details[1]] -> that occupies transition floors,
[transition floor.details[2]] -> causing adventurers to hunger at a
[transition floor.details[3]] -> much slower rate than normal.
[transition floor.details[4]] -> The perfect spot to take a break.
[transition floor.details[6]] -> Be warned, mimics may still take
[transition floor.details[7]] -> the place of treasure chests here.
[transition floor.details[9]] -> The transition floor between the
[transition floor.details[10]] -> mines and swamps contains a hidden
[transition floor.details[11]] -> portal to the underworld.
[transition floor.details[12]] -> If one wishes to risk a visit, some
[transition floor.details[13]] -> method of digging is needed.
[underworld.blurb[0]] -> These catacombs are the first destination
[underworld.blurb[1]] -> for souls who have recently died.
[underworld.blurb[3]] -> Depending on how they lived, the other
[underworld.blurb[4]] -> denizens of the Underworld may cast them
[underworld.blurb[5]] -> further down into Hell.
[underworld.details[0]] -> INHABITANTS:
[underworld.details[1]] -> Skeletons, Slimes, Ghouls, Imps,
[underworld.details[2]] -> Shadows
[underworld.details[4]] -> SECRET LEVEL TREASURES:
[underworld.details[5]] -> - Khryselakatos (Lvl 7)
[underworld.details[7]] -> The underworld can be accessed twice
[underworld.details[8]] -> via secret entrances on floor 5 and 18.
[underworld.details[9]] -> In both cases, adventurers who find
[underworld.details[10]] -> a trapdoor down to a second floor of
[underworld.details[11]] -> the underworld will find a deadly
[underworld.details[12]] -> reward awaiting them.
[underworld.details[14]] -> Beware, most foes attack across pits.
[cauldron.blurb[0]] -> Whether you need to boil potion
[cauldron.blurb[1]] -> mixtures, or cook up a hot meal,
[cauldron.blurb[2]] -> the sturdy CAULDRON is a practical
[cauldron.blurb[3]] -> fixture for any facility.
[cauldron.blurb[4]] -> Shame it's too heavy
[cauldron.blurb[5]] -> to take along with you!
[cauldron.details[0]] -> Finding a cauldron is an opportunity
[cauldron.details[1]] -> for any adventurer, whether or not
[cauldron.details[2]] -> they are skilled in alchemy, to ease
[cauldron.details[3]] -> pressure on inventory space. Cooking
[cauldron.details[4]] -> consolidates any food into rations,
[cauldron.details[5]] -> while decanting consolidates potions.
[cauldron.details[7]] -> Combining potions and rations allows
[cauldron.details[8]] -> for the creation of flavored food
[cauldron.details[9]] -> which can enhance adventurer stats.
[cauldron.details[11]] -> Those with 80 or more skill in alchemy
[cauldron.details[12]] -> are able to make fresh rations, safe
[cauldron.details[13]] -> from the perils of indigestion.
[workbench.blurb[0]] -> While not as convenient as the portable
[workbench.blurb[1]] -> tinkering kit, the WORKBENCH has all the
[workbench.blurb[2]] -> same tools available for resourceful
[workbench.blurb[3]] -> adventurers to fashion useful items for
[workbench.blurb[4]] -> the obstacles which lie ahead.
[workbench.details[0]] -> As a sturdier table and set of heftier
[workbench.details[1]] -> tools, workbenches do not degrade,
[workbench.details[2]] -> making it an efficient find, even if
[workbench.details[3]] -> carrying a tinkering kit.
[workbench.details[5]] -> Many adventurers may benefit from
[workbench.details[6]] -> occasional tinkering, particularly
[workbench.details[7]] -> for keeping tools handy, like
[workbench.details[8]] -> empty flasks, lockpicks, or traps.
[workbench.details[10]] -> As only the mechanist class starts with
[workbench.details[11]] -> the kit, but several others have some
[workbench.details[12]] -> tinkering skill, the workbench allows
[workbench.details[13]] -> broader use of tinkering tools.
[button.blurb[0]] -> Like the lever, BUTTONS can be pressed
[button.blurb[1]] -> manually, but may also be struck from
[button.blurb[2]] -> afar with projectiles to activate
[button.blurb[3]] -> dungeon mechanisms.
[button.blurb[4]] -> Some are designed to reset after a time.
[button.details[0]] -> Not much needs to be said about the
[button.details[1]] -> humble dungeon button.
[button.details[3]] -> Architects may prefer buttons over
[button.details[4]] -> levers, as no clear floor space is
[button.details[5]] -> required, and buttons are easier
[button.details[6]] -> to hide on walls where outsiders
[button.details[7]] -> are not intended to access.
[button.details[9]] -> Beware a button which resets, as
[button.details[10]] -> it usually heralds a puzzle, or
[button.details[11]] -> perhaps a trap for the careless.
[wall locks.blurb[0]] -> Usually used to secure impenetrable iron
[wall locks.blurb[1]] -> doors, the WALL LOCK requires a key made
[wall locks.blurb[2]] -> from matching materials.
[wall locks.blurb[3]] -> Locks may operate other dungeon gadgets
[wall locks.blurb[4]] -> and, in some cases, may be toggled to
[wall locks.blurb[5]] -> activate and deactivate a gadget.
[wall locks.details[0]] -> As iron doors are most often used to
[wall locks.details[1]] -> guard precious items or gold, keys are
[wall locks.details[2]] -> often traded for treasures.
[wall locks.details[3]] -> Adventurers should make use of the
[wall locks.details[4]] -> handy window installed in iron doors
[wall locks.details[5]] -> to first peek at the prize within,
[wall locks.details[6]] -> presuming they're tall enough.
[wall locks.details[8]] -> Iron, Bronze, and some Silver locks
[wall locks.details[9]] -> may be picked by sufficiently skilled
[wall locks.details[10]] -> Tinkerers, or with a Skeleton Key.
[wall locks.details[11]] -> But as the value of the treasure
[wall locks.details[12]] -> increases with the depth of the
[wall locks.details[13]] -> dungeon, so too does security.
[arcane boulder.blurb[0]] -> Though boulders are already a deadly
[arcane boulder.blurb[1]] -> hazard, concentrations of crystal 
[arcane boulder.blurb[2]] -> imbues them with dangerous magic.
[arcane boulder.blurb[4]] -> Arcane boulders roll with enhanced speed
[arcane boulder.blurb[5]] -> and momentum, defying physical laws.
[arcane boulder.details[0]] -> The most deadly boulder trap, those
[arcane boulder.details[1]] -> who live long enough to face these
[arcane boulder.details[2]] -> imposing orbs should be adept at
[arcane boulder.details[3]] -> avoiding them.
[arcane boulder.details[5]] -> Beware, they fall and roll much
[arcane boulder.details[6]] -> faster, and can roll over liquid
[arcane boulder.details[7]] -> and pits unimpeded, and their
[arcane boulder.details[8]] -> crushing power is enhanced with
[arcane boulder.details[9]] -> a magical detonation.
[arcane boulder.details[11]] -> Those with Push or Telekinesis may
[arcane boulder.details[12]] -> be able to put these magical
[arcane boulder.details[13]] -> qualities to use.
[assist shrine.blurb[0]] -> The ASSIST SHRINE did not always grace
[assist shrine.blurb[1]] -> the Minehead entry. The Church claims the
[assist shrine.blurb[2]] -> Eternals placed it there to:
[assist shrine.blurb[3]] -> ''Bless the courageous to defeat Herx and
[assist shrine.blurb[4]] -> end his curse; Give hope to the hopeless.''
[assist shrine.blurb[5]] -> (for better or worse)
[assist shrine.details[0]] -> When claiming items from the assist
[assist shrine.details[1]] -> shrine, a party should be aware that
[assist shrine.details[2]] -> they will be judged according to the
[assist shrine.details[3]] -> sum total of assistance taken.
[assist shrine.details[4]] -> For parties with mixed expertise, this
[assist shrine.details[5]] -> can allow stronger adventurers to
[assist shrine.details[6]] -> bear the full challenge, while novices
[assist shrine.details[7]] -> face a much less daunting challenge.
[assist shrine.details[9]] -> Adventuring solo, even novice heroes
[assist shrine.details[10]] -> can accomplish great feats by taking
[assist shrine.details[11]] -> much more assistance.
[assist shrine.details[13]] -> There is no shame in doing so!

